et⠀named.⠀Disagreement⠀and⠀uncertainty⠀belong⠀to⠀the⠀relationship,⠀not⠀as⠀obstacles⠀to⠀be⠀defeated⠀but⠀as⠀moments⠀where⠀the⠀characters⠀reveal⠀what⠀they⠀want⠀and⠀what⠀they⠀are⠀afraid⠀to⠀risk.⠀Let⠀timing,⠀obligations,⠀and⠀competing⠀wants⠀create⠀complications⠀with⠀meaningful⠀aftermath.\n\nLet⠀an⠀installment⠀register⠀ordinary⠀absence⠀and⠀return⠀without⠀forcing⠀a⠀resolution.⠀A⠀character⠀can⠀miss⠀a⠀usual⠀detail⠀or⠀notice⠀that⠀it⠀is⠀finally⠀back;⠀the⠀absence⠀itself⠀carries⠀part⠀of⠀the⠀relationship's⠀history.⠀Progress⠀can⠀involve⠀knowledge,⠀relationships,⠀work,⠀or⠀resources.⠀The⠀installment⠀can⠀close⠀on⠀completed⠀work,⠀a⠀pending⠀request,⠀or⠀plain⠀acknowledgment⠀of⠀what⠀is⠀now⠀known.⠀Serial⠀duration⠀should⠀give⠀selected⠀facts⠀room⠀to⠀acquire⠀meaning,⠀not⠀make⠀a⠀fair⠀answer⠀perpetually⠀recede.⠀The⠀style⠀does⠀not⠀automatically⠀create⠀leveling⠀systems,⠀rankings,⠀or⠀progression-fantasy⠀world⠀rules.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajaa::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Angsty⠀/⠀Emotionally⠀Turbulent\n\nWrite⠀the⠀relationship⠀through⠀the⠀pressure⠀that⠀ordinary⠀routines⠀put⠀on⠀unresolved⠀hurt.⠀Let⠀a⠀practical⠀activity—cooking,⠀waiting⠀for⠀a⠀train,⠀sorting⠀a⠀room,⠀walking⠀a⠀familiar⠀route—carry⠀the⠀weight⠀of⠀what⠀one⠀person⠀cannot⠀say⠀or⠀what⠀the⠀other⠀cannot⠀stop⠀remembering.⠀Describe⠀the⠀activity⠀itself⠀calmly⠀and⠀precisely;⠀place⠀the⠀turbulence⠀in⠀the⠀gap⠀between⠀that⠀even⠀surface⠀and⠀the⠀private⠀reaction⠀pressing⠀against⠀it.\n\nGive⠀each⠀person⠀a⠀specific⠀reason⠀for⠀withholding⠀or⠀exposing⠀feeling.⠀One⠀may⠀speak⠀too⠀much⠀about⠀a⠀small⠀thing⠀because⠀the⠀larger⠀admission⠀is⠀impossible;⠀the⠀other⠀may⠀answer⠀with⠀practical⠀help⠀because⠀that⠀is⠀the⠀only⠀care⠀available.⠀Let⠀the⠀strain⠀alter⠀the⠀actual⠀conversation:⠀a⠀question⠀arrives⠀late,⠀an⠀apology⠀turns⠀into⠀an⠀instruction,⠀a⠀needed⠀sentence⠀is⠀replaced⠀by⠀a⠀detail⠀about⠀the⠀weather⠀or⠀a⠀cup⠀left⠀on⠀a⠀table.⠀Do⠀not⠀make⠀the⠀dialogue⠀uniformly⠀raw⠀or⠀confessional.⠀The⠀most⠀damaging⠀moment⠀can⠀be⠀a⠀quiet⠀one.\n\nUse⠀the⠀narrator's⠀distance⠀to⠀show⠀the⠀cost⠀of⠀closeness.⠀A⠀character⠀can⠀notice⠀the⠀exact⠀position⠀of⠀another⠀person's⠀hands,⠀the⠀sound⠀of⠀a⠀door⠀closing,⠀or⠀the⠀time⠀between⠀a⠀question⠀and⠀its⠀answer,⠀and⠀that⠀noticing⠀becomes⠀the⠀evidence⠀of⠀how⠀much⠀the⠀relationship⠀matters.⠀Private⠀thought⠀may⠀return⠀to⠀the⠀same⠀memory⠀or⠀phrase⠀without⠀resolving⠀it.⠀Uncertainty⠀about⠀whether⠀to⠀stay,⠀return,⠀apologize,⠀or⠀stop⠀hoping⠀can⠀remain⠀active⠀across⠀the⠀scene.\n\nLet⠀comfort⠀be⠀partial⠀or⠀awkward⠀when⠀it⠀appears.⠀Warmth⠀may⠀arrive⠀through⠀a⠀small⠀accurate⠀gesture—a⠀remembered⠀preference,⠀a⠀blanket⠀placed⠀without⠀comment,⠀a⠀message⠀sent⠀and⠀then⠀regretted—without⠀erasing⠀the⠀pain⠀or⠀forcing⠀a⠀clean⠀resolution.⠀The⠀relationship⠀should⠀feel⠀like⠀a⠀particular⠀connection⠀between⠀two⠀people,⠀not⠀a⠀generic⠀cycle⠀of⠀hurt⠀and⠀reconciliation.⠀End⠀where⠀the⠀emotional⠀pressure⠀is⠀most⠀alive;⠀whether⠀anything⠀has⠀been⠀settled⠀is⠀left⠀to⠀the⠀story.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajab::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Chat⠀Roleplay\n\nWrite⠀the⠀shared⠀interval⠀in⠀clear,⠀readable⠀paragraphs⠀with⠀unmistakable⠀dialogue⠀attribution.⠀Keep⠀each⠀paragraph⠀focused⠀enough⠀that⠀a⠀reader⠀can⠀follow⠀who⠀is⠀speaking⠀and⠀what⠀is⠀happening⠀without⠀rereading.⠀Use⠀short⠀narrative⠀passages⠀to⠀establish⠀the⠀practical⠀setting—a⠀kitchen,⠀a⠀station⠀platform,⠀a⠀quiet⠀street,⠀a⠀room⠀where⠀someone⠀is⠀waiting—and⠀let⠀the⠀characters⠀move⠀through⠀it⠀naturally.\n\nBring⠀Murakami's⠀calm⠀attention⠀into⠀the⠀collaborative⠀scene⠀through⠀specific⠀ordinary⠀details:⠀the⠀weight⠀of⠀a⠀bag,⠀the⠀sound⠀of⠀water⠀running,⠀the⠀way⠀one⠀person⠀looks⠀at⠀a⠀clock⠀or⠀a⠀window.⠀Let⠀those⠀details⠀carry⠀private⠀concern⠀without⠀requiring⠀a⠀long⠀interior⠀passage.⠀When⠀a⠀character⠀thinks⠀or⠀feels⠀something,⠀place⠀it⠀close⠀to⠀the⠀action⠀or⠀speech⠀that⠀prompts⠀it,⠀so⠀the⠀scene⠀remains⠀easy⠀to⠀follow.\n\nDevelop⠀the⠀romantic⠀connection⠀through⠀attention,⠀memory,⠀and⠀small⠀decisions⠀rather⠀than⠀generic⠀flirting.⠀One⠀character⠀may⠀remember⠀a⠀preference⠀the⠀other⠀mentioned⠀earlier,⠀choose⠀to⠀stay⠀a⠀little⠀longer,⠀or⠀notice⠀something⠀the⠀other⠀is⠀trying⠀to⠀hide.⠀Let⠀timing⠀and⠀competing⠀obligations⠀create⠀natural⠀friction.⠀The⠀scene⠀does⠀not⠀need⠀to⠀reach⠀a⠀confession⠀or⠀a⠀resolution;⠀it⠀needs⠀to⠀make⠀the⠀connection⠀feel⠀particular⠀and⠀alive.\n\nEnd⠀at⠀a⠀natural⠀continuation⠀point⠀that⠀follows⠀from⠀what⠀has⠀just⠀happened.⠀The⠀next⠀reply⠀may⠀pick⠀up⠀the⠀conversation,⠀continue⠀an⠀action,⠀or⠀enter⠀a⠀new⠀interval.⠀Do⠀not⠀force⠀a⠀question,⠀cliffhanger,⠀or⠀choice⠀at⠀the⠀end.⠀Preserve⠀the⠀active⠀narrator,⠀person,⠀action⠀markers,⠀and⠀player⠀control⠀from⠀the⠀supplied⠀settings.⠀Keep⠀ongoing⠀world⠀and⠀NPC⠀behavior⠀active⠀without⠀requiring⠀the⠀scene⠀to⠀pause⠀or⠀change⠀direction⠀before⠀the⠀response⠀ends.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajac::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Chinese⠀Literary⠀Traditions\n\nUse⠀the⠀intimate⠀urban⠀or⠀domestic⠀narrative⠀route⠀from⠀the⠀Chinese⠀literary⠀traditions⠀profile.⠀Tell⠀the⠀relationship⠀through⠀close⠀attention⠀to⠀the⠀spaces⠀where⠀the⠀characters⠀live,⠀work,⠀meet,⠀and⠀wait:⠀a⠀small⠀apartment,⠀a⠀family⠀shop,⠀a⠀teahouse,⠀a⠀neighborhood⠀street,⠀a⠀room⠀that⠀changes⠀meaning⠀because⠀of⠀who⠀enters⠀or⠀leaves⠀it.⠀Keep⠀the⠀setting⠀concrete⠀and⠀particular⠀to⠀the⠀community⠀actually⠀supplied⠀in⠀the⠀scene.\n\nLet⠀Murakami's⠀calm⠀routine⠀shape⠀the⠀domestic⠀rhythm.⠀Describe⠀practical⠀activities—preparing⠀food,⠀cleaning,⠀walking⠀to⠀a⠀bus⠀stop,⠀closing⠀a⠀window,⠀sorting⠀papers—with⠀even,⠀unhurried⠀precision.⠀Let⠀those⠀activities⠀become⠀the⠀surface⠀across⠀which⠀the⠀relationship⠀moves.⠀A⠀character's⠀attention⠀to⠀a⠀small⠀domestic⠀detail⠀can⠀reveal⠀care,⠀hesitation,⠀or⠀the⠀pressure⠀of⠀something⠀unspoken⠀without⠀announcing⠀it.\n\nDevelop⠀the⠀romantic⠀connection⠀through⠀proximity⠀and⠀the⠀obligations⠀of⠀shared⠀or⠀neighboring⠀life.⠀The⠀characters⠀may⠀be⠀brought⠀together⠀by⠀family⠀expectations,⠀work,⠀housing,⠀or⠀a⠀mutual⠀acquaintance,⠀but⠀the⠀relationship⠀itself⠀should⠀grow⠀through⠀particular⠀choices:⠀a⠀meal⠀prepared⠀for⠀someone,⠀a⠀visit⠀that⠀lasts⠀longer⠀than⠀intended,⠀a⠀confidence⠀offered⠀or⠀withheld,⠀a⠀disagreement⠀about⠀how⠀to⠀handle⠀a⠀practical⠀problem.⠀Let⠀the⠀aftermath⠀of⠀those⠀moments⠀accumulate⠀across⠀the⠀scene.\n\nKeep⠀the⠀narration⠀close⠀to⠀the⠀chosen⠀viewpoint⠀character's⠀perception⠀and⠀private⠀concern.⠀The⠀prose⠀may⠀move⠀between⠀outward⠀domestic⠀detail⠀and⠀inward⠀reflection⠀without⠀abandoning⠀the⠀scene.⠀Use⠀the⠀period,⠀language,⠀and⠀community⠀already⠀supplied.⠀The⠀intimacy⠀should⠀feel⠀culturally⠀situated⠀through⠀concrete⠀daily⠀life,⠀not⠀through⠀a⠀generic⠀list⠀of⠀family,⠀work,⠀and⠀money⠀pressures.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajad::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Compressed⠀Gritty⠀Prose\n\nWrite⠀the⠀relationship⠀through⠀concrete⠀physical⠀detail⠀and⠀compressed⠀movement.⠀Keep⠀transitions⠀short⠀and⠀direct:⠀one⠀action⠀follows⠀another⠀without⠀explanatory⠀padding.⠀Describe⠀what⠀the⠀characters⠀handle,⠀carry,⠀repair,⠀or⠀wear⠀down—a⠀cracked⠀cup,⠀a⠀coat⠀with⠀a⠀torn⠀lining,⠀a⠀door⠀that⠀sticks,⠀a⠀phone⠀with⠀a⠀damaged⠀screen.⠀Let⠀those⠀material⠀facts⠀carry⠀the⠀weight⠀of⠀the⠀relationship's⠀history⠀and⠀present⠀strain.\n\nUse⠀forceful,⠀plain⠀diction.⠀Name⠀the⠀action⠀and⠀its⠀cost.⠀A⠀character⠀may⠀set⠀down⠀a⠀bag⠀too⠀hard,⠀wait⠀in⠀a⠀cold⠀stairwell,⠀or⠀say⠀something⠀sharp⠀while⠀doing⠀a⠀necessary⠀task.⠀Ground⠀rough⠀or⠀abrasive⠀speech⠀in⠀the⠀particular⠀speaker⠀and⠀situation;⠀do⠀not⠀make⠀every⠀exchange⠀combative.⠀The⠀romance⠀should⠀feel⠀earned⠀through⠀practical⠀care⠀and⠀physical⠀proximity,⠀not⠀through⠀soft⠀language.\n\nLet⠀Murakami's⠀attention⠀to⠀ordinary⠀things⠀become⠀high-contrast⠀rather⠀than⠀dreamy.⠀A⠀familiar⠀object⠀can⠀appear⠀with⠀sudden⠀clarity⠀because⠀the⠀character⠀is⠀tired,⠀worried,⠀or⠀trying⠀not⠀to⠀look⠀at⠀the⠀other⠀person.⠀Keep⠀private⠀concern⠀close⠀to⠀the⠀physical⠀scene:⠀a⠀thought⠀about⠀leaving⠀can⠀arrive⠀while⠀someone⠀is⠀washing⠀a⠀dish⠀or⠀checking⠀a⠀lock.⠀Do⠀not⠀let⠀the⠀compressed⠀style⠀erase⠀interiority;⠀retain⠀a⠀longer⠀thought⠀when⠀the⠀character's⠀reasoning⠀needs⠀it.\n\nChange⠀rhythm⠀deliberately.⠀A⠀sequence⠀of⠀short,⠀hard⠀actions⠀can⠀open⠀into⠀a⠀slower⠀moment⠀of⠀attention⠀or⠀speech,⠀then⠀tighten⠀again.⠀The⠀relationship⠀advances⠀through⠀decisions⠀with⠀physical⠀consequences:⠀staying,⠀leaving,⠀touching,⠀refusing⠀to⠀touch,⠀handing⠀something⠀over,⠀taking⠀it⠀back.⠀End⠀where⠀the⠀scene's⠀physical⠀and⠀emotional⠀pressure⠀is⠀most⠀alive;⠀whether⠀anything⠀resolves⠀is⠀left⠀to⠀the⠀story.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajae::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Epistolary⠀/⠀Documents\n\nTell⠀the⠀relationship⠀through⠀documents,⠀each⠀with⠀a⠀clear⠀author,⠀intended⠀recipient⠀or⠀purpose,⠀and⠀time⠀of⠀composition.⠀Use⠀the⠀specific⠀document⠀form⠀the⠀scene⠀requires:⠀a⠀letter,⠀a⠀journal⠀entry,⠀a⠀note⠀left⠀on⠀a⠀table,⠀a⠀message,⠀a⠀list,⠀a⠀report,⠀or⠀another⠀written⠀record.⠀Do⠀not⠀rotate⠀through⠀formats⠀mechanically;⠀choose⠀the⠀form⠀that⠀fits⠀what⠀the⠀character⠀would⠀actually⠀write⠀in⠀that⠀situation.\n\nLet⠀each⠀document⠀carry⠀Murakami's⠀calm⠀attention⠀to⠀ordinary⠀things.⠀A⠀writer⠀may⠀describe⠀a⠀meal,⠀a⠀walk,⠀the⠀weather,⠀a⠀room,⠀or⠀an⠀object⠀in⠀precise⠀detail⠀while⠀the⠀real⠀concern⠀remains⠀only⠀partly⠀stated.⠀The⠀gap⠀between⠀the⠀recorded⠀detail⠀and⠀the⠀unrecorded⠀feeling⠀is⠀part⠀of⠀the⠀relationship.⠀What⠀a⠀document⠀knows⠀or⠀conceals⠀follows⠀its⠀author's⠀situation:⠀one⠀person⠀may⠀write⠀too⠀much⠀about⠀a⠀small⠀thing⠀to⠀avoid⠀a⠀larger⠀admission;⠀another⠀may⠀record⠀only⠀practical⠀information⠀because⠀that⠀is⠀the⠀only⠀safe⠀communication.\n\nUse⠀gaps,⠀revisions,⠀and⠀conflicting⠀accounts⠀to⠀reveal⠀the⠀relationship⠀across⠀entries.⠀A⠀letter⠀may⠀be⠀drafted⠀and⠀never⠀sent;⠀a⠀journal⠀entry⠀may⠀be⠀crossed⠀out⠀or⠀resumed⠀days⠀later;⠀two⠀people⠀may⠀remember⠀the⠀same⠀evening⠀differently.⠀Let⠀those⠀differences⠀show⠀their⠀particular⠀hopes,⠀fears,⠀and⠀misunderstandings⠀without⠀adding⠀an⠀omniscient⠀explanation⠀after⠀every⠀record.⠀Preserve⠀readable⠀continuity⠀by⠀letting⠀each⠀document⠀respond⠀to⠀or⠀anticipate⠀the⠀others.\n\nKeep⠀the⠀romance⠀legible⠀through⠀attention,⠀memory,⠀and⠀decisions⠀about⠀belonging⠀together.⠀A⠀document⠀may⠀preserve⠀a⠀shared⠀moment,⠀ask⠀a⠀question,⠀offer⠀care,⠀or⠀record⠀a⠀decision⠀to⠀stay⠀or⠀leave.⠀Uncertainty⠀can⠀remain⠀unresolved:⠀a⠀letter⠀may⠀end⠀without⠀the⠀sentence⠀its⠀writer⠀intended,⠀and⠀the⠀next⠀document⠀may⠀not⠀answer⠀it.⠀Compose⠀the⠀story⠀entirely⠀as⠀documents;⠀do⠀not⠀turn⠀them⠀into⠀summaries⠀of⠀a⠀scene⠀that⠀happens⠀elsewhere.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajaf::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Fluffy⠀/⠀Comforting\n\nWrite⠀the⠀relationship⠀through⠀chosen⠀kindness⠀and⠀the⠀ease⠀of⠀being⠀known.⠀Let⠀one⠀character⠀remember⠀a⠀familiar⠀preference—how⠀the⠀other⠀takes⠀tea,⠀which⠀route⠀they⠀prefer,⠀what⠀they⠀do⠀when⠀they⠀cannot⠀sleep—and⠀act⠀on⠀it⠀without⠀making⠀a⠀display.⠀The⠀care⠀should⠀feel⠀particular⠀to⠀these⠀people,⠀not⠀a⠀generic⠀gesture.\n\nUse⠀Murakami's⠀unhurried⠀practical⠀activities⠀as⠀the⠀medium⠀for⠀warmth.⠀A⠀meal⠀prepared⠀slowly,⠀a⠀coat⠀hung⠀up,⠀a⠀book⠀left⠀open⠀at⠀the⠀right⠀page,⠀a⠀quiet⠀walk⠀taken⠀together,⠀a⠀room⠀made⠀comfortable⠀before⠀the⠀other⠀arrives:⠀these⠀small⠀actions⠀carry⠀the⠀affection.⠀Describe⠀them⠀with⠀calm,⠀even⠀attention,⠀letting⠀the⠀pleasure⠀of⠀the⠀ordinary⠀moment⠀be⠀enough.⠀The⠀scene⠀does⠀not⠀need⠀a⠀confession⠀or⠀an⠀emotional⠀repair⠀to⠀be⠀meaningful.\n\nKeep⠀personality,⠀privacy,⠀and⠀disagreement⠀intact.⠀Comfort⠀does⠀not⠀make⠀everyone⠀agreeable.⠀One⠀character⠀may⠀be⠀tired,⠀distracted,⠀or⠀quietly⠀stubborn;⠀the⠀other⠀may⠀offer⠀care⠀in⠀a⠀way⠀that⠀respects⠀that⠀mood⠀rather⠀than⠀demanding⠀gratitude.⠀Let⠀affection⠀be⠀sincere⠀without⠀requiring⠀every⠀feeling⠀to⠀be⠀spoken.⠀Private⠀thought⠀may⠀hold⠀a⠀warmth⠀the⠀character⠀does⠀not⠀yet⠀say⠀aloud.\n\nLet⠀small⠀pleasures⠀have⠀room⠀to⠀breathe:⠀a⠀shared⠀meal,⠀a⠀familiar⠀song,⠀a⠀comfortable⠀silence,⠀a⠀joke⠀that⠀only⠀the⠀two⠀of⠀them⠀understand.⠀The⠀relationship⠀should⠀feel⠀like⠀a⠀particular⠀connection⠀with⠀its⠀own⠀history⠀and⠀rhythm.⠀End⠀where⠀the⠀scene⠀naturally⠀pauses,⠀even⠀if⠀the⠀larger⠀situation⠀remains⠀unfinished;⠀whether⠀anything⠀resolves⠀is⠀left⠀to⠀the⠀story.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajag::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Formal⠀Literary⠀Novel\n\nWrite⠀the⠀relationship⠀in⠀composed⠀novel⠀prose⠀with⠀deliberate⠀transitions⠀and⠀sustained⠀paragraph⠀movement.⠀Let⠀each⠀scene⠀open⠀into⠀its⠀social⠀and⠀physical⠀setting—a⠀neighborhood,⠀a⠀workplace,⠀a⠀family⠀home,⠀a⠀city⠀street—and⠀let⠀that⠀context⠀frame⠀what⠀the⠀characters⠀can⠀say⠀or⠀do.⠀Use⠀narrative⠀distance⠀where⠀the⠀chosen⠀narrator⠀permits⠀it:⠀the⠀narration⠀may⠀observe⠀how⠀a⠀room⠀has⠀changed,⠀what⠀a⠀particular⠀street⠀means⠀to⠀the⠀people⠀who⠀live⠀there,⠀or⠀how⠀an⠀obligation⠀shapes⠀a⠀private⠀decision.\n\nKeep⠀Murakami's⠀unhurried⠀practical⠀attention⠀inside⠀the⠀formal⠀architecture.⠀Describe⠀ordinary⠀activities—preparing⠀a⠀meal,⠀walking⠀to⠀an⠀appointment,⠀waiting⠀for⠀a⠀call,⠀clearing⠀a⠀table—with⠀even⠀precision,⠀and⠀let⠀those⠀activities⠀carry⠀associations⠀with⠀private⠀concern.⠀The⠀strangeness⠀of⠀a⠀familiar⠀moment⠀can⠀emerge⠀through⠀exact⠀detail:⠀a⠀sound⠀heard⠀at⠀the⠀wrong⠀time,⠀an⠀object⠀found⠀in⠀an⠀unexpected⠀place,⠀a⠀silence⠀that⠀lasts⠀too⠀long.⠀Do⠀not⠀turn⠀the⠀scene⠀into⠀literal⠀impossibility;⠀keep⠀the⠀account⠀psychologically⠀unsettled⠀where⠀the⠀world⠀does⠀not⠀permit⠀more.\n\nDevelop⠀the⠀romance⠀through⠀the⠀relationship's⠀particular⠀history⠀and⠀social⠀situation.⠀The⠀characters⠀may⠀be⠀shaped⠀by⠀family⠀expectations,⠀work,⠀reputation,⠀or⠀a⠀shared⠀past,⠀but⠀the⠀connection⠀itself⠀should⠀grow⠀through⠀specific⠀choices:⠀a⠀visit⠀made⠀or⠀avoided,⠀a⠀confidence⠀offered,⠀a⠀disagreement⠀about⠀what⠀they⠀owe⠀other⠀people,⠀a⠀decision⠀to⠀stay⠀or⠀leave.⠀Let⠀the⠀aftermath⠀of⠀those⠀choices⠀accumulate⠀across⠀paragraphs⠀rather⠀than⠀resolving⠀in⠀a⠀single⠀exchange.\n\nDistinguish⠀narration⠀from⠀ordinary⠀spoken⠀language.⠀The⠀prose⠀may⠀frame⠀a⠀moment⠀through⠀judgment,⠀memory,⠀or⠀social⠀observation,⠀but⠀it⠀should⠀remain⠀grounded⠀in⠀the⠀chosen⠀viewpoint⠀character's⠀access⠀and⠀knowledge.⠀Private⠀thought⠀may⠀be⠀extensive⠀or⠀brief⠀depending⠀on⠀the⠀character⠀and⠀the⠀pressure⠀of⠀the⠀scene.⠀End⠀where⠀the⠀formal⠀movement⠀of⠀the⠀scene⠀reaches⠀a⠀natural⠀pause,⠀even⠀if⠀the⠀relationship⠀remains⠀unsettled.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajah::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Framed⠀Oral⠀Storytelling⠀(Arabian⠀Nights-inspired)\n\nWrite⠀the⠀romance⠀as⠀a⠀courtship⠀conducted⠀partly⠀through⠀stories⠀one⠀character⠀tells⠀another.⠀Give⠀each⠀telling⠀a⠀concrete⠀occasion:⠀a⠀long⠀walk,⠀a⠀meal⠀prepared⠀together,⠀a⠀wait⠀for⠀a⠀delayed⠀train,⠀an⠀evening⠀when⠀neither⠀wants⠀to⠀go⠀home.⠀The⠀listener⠀has⠀a⠀reason⠀to⠀keep⠀asking,⠀and⠀the⠀teller⠀has⠀a⠀reason⠀to⠀keep⠀choosing⠀what⠀to⠀reveal.\n\nLet⠀the⠀embedded⠀story⠀be⠀an⠀indirect⠀disclosure.⠀The⠀teller⠀recounts⠀a⠀past⠀journey,⠀a⠀former⠀attachment,⠀a⠀strange⠀encounter,⠀or⠀a⠀small⠀failure,⠀and⠀the⠀listener⠀hears⠀something⠀about⠀the⠀teller's⠀present⠀capacity⠀for⠀attention,⠀loyalty,⠀or⠀avoidance.⠀The⠀outer⠀scene⠀should⠀register⠀the⠀listener's⠀response⠀in⠀concrete⠀terms:⠀a⠀question⠀asked⠀too⠀late,⠀a⠀hand⠀that⠀stays⠀near⠀but⠀does⠀not⠀touch,⠀a⠀change⠀in⠀how⠀they⠀watch⠀the⠀teller⠀afterward.⠀The⠀relationship⠀advances⠀or⠀stalls⠀because⠀of⠀what⠀the⠀story⠀makes⠀legible⠀between⠀them,⠀not⠀because⠀the⠀story⠀itself⠀contains⠀a⠀confession.\n\nUse⠀Murakami's⠀unhurried⠀practical⠀texture⠀inside⠀both⠀levels.⠀The⠀outer⠀scene⠀can⠀move⠀through⠀ordinary⠀actions—washing⠀dishes,⠀folding⠀laundry,⠀walking⠀to⠀a⠀convenience⠀store,⠀waiting⠀for⠀water⠀to⠀boil—while⠀the⠀embedded⠀story⠀unfolds⠀at⠀the⠀same⠀calm⠀pace.⠀Let⠀an⠀ordinary⠀object⠀in⠀the⠀present⠀scene⠀echo⠀something⠀from⠀the⠀told⠀story:⠀a⠀scar⠀on⠀a⠀kettle,⠀a⠀particular⠀brand⠀of⠀cigarettes,⠀the⠀sound⠀of⠀a⠀bicycle⠀passing.⠀The⠀echo⠀should⠀feel⠀like⠀private⠀association,⠀not⠀magical⠀correspondence.⠀Keep⠀strangeness⠀evenly⠀described:⠀if⠀the⠀told⠀story⠀contains⠀an⠀uncanny⠀detail,⠀neither⠀the⠀teller⠀nor⠀the⠀listener⠀treats⠀it⠀as⠀more⠀than⠀a⠀fact⠀that⠀has⠀not⠀been⠀explained.\n\nManage⠀the⠀narrative⠀levels⠀clearly.⠀The⠀outer⠀scene⠀uses⠀the⠀story's⠀main⠀narration.⠀The⠀embedded⠀story⠀may⠀be⠀rendered⠀as⠀continuous⠀quoted⠀telling,⠀as⠀paraphrase⠀with⠀occasional⠀direct⠀lines,⠀or⠀as⠀a⠀shift⠀into⠀a⠀clearly⠀marked⠀inset⠀passage.⠀Whichever⠀form⠀you⠀choose,⠀keep⠀it⠀consistent⠀within⠀the⠀scene.⠀When⠀the⠀telling⠀is⠀interrupted—by⠀a⠀question,⠀a⠀phone⠀call,⠀a⠀task⠀that⠀needs⠀attention—return⠀to⠀the⠀outer⠀level⠀and⠀let⠀the⠀interruption⠀change⠀the⠀telling's⠀rhythm.\n\nLet⠀recurrence⠀accrue⠀romantic⠀meaning.⠀A⠀phrase⠀the⠀teller⠀repeats,⠀an⠀image⠀that⠀appears⠀in⠀both⠀levels,⠀or⠀a⠀question⠀the⠀listener⠀asks⠀more⠀than⠀once⠀should⠀gather⠀weight⠀through⠀the⠀scene.⠀The⠀repetition⠀can⠀mark⠀growing⠀trust,⠀a⠀hesitation⠀neither⠀names,⠀or⠀the⠀listener's⠀attempt⠀to⠀understand⠀something⠀the⠀teller⠀will⠀not⠀say⠀directly.⠀Do⠀not⠀force⠀the⠀repeated⠀element⠀to⠀resolve⠀into⠀a⠀symbol;⠀let⠀it⠀remain⠀a⠀detail⠀both⠀characters⠀notice⠀without⠀fully⠀explaining.\n\nPreserve⠀the⠀difference⠀between⠀what⠀the⠀teller⠀knows⠀and⠀what⠀the⠀listener⠀understands.⠀The⠀teller⠀may⠀be⠀telling⠀the⠀story⠀to⠀delay⠀a⠀decision,⠀to⠀test⠀the⠀listener's⠀patience,⠀to⠀offer⠀a⠀version⠀of⠀the⠀past⠀that⠀flatters⠀or⠀protects⠀someone,⠀or⠀simply⠀because⠀the⠀story⠀is⠀the⠀only⠀way⠀they⠀know⠀to⠀say⠀what⠀they⠀feel.⠀The⠀listener⠀may⠀hear⠀more⠀or⠀less⠀than⠀the⠀teller⠀intends.⠀Neither⠀character⠀should⠀become⠀a⠀perfect⠀reader⠀of⠀the⠀other.⠀Let⠀the⠀romance⠀develop⠀through⠀the⠀accumulating⠀mismatch⠀and⠀alignment⠀between⠀what⠀is⠀told⠀and⠀what⠀is⠀received.\n\nEnd⠀the⠀scene⠀at⠀a⠀natural⠀threshold:⠀the⠀story⠀finishes,⠀the⠀walk⠀reaches⠀its⠀destination,⠀the⠀meal⠀is⠀cleared,⠀or⠀the⠀listener⠀asks⠀a⠀question⠀the⠀teller⠀has⠀not⠀yet⠀answered.⠀The⠀relationship⠀does⠀not⠀need⠀to⠀resolve.⠀What⠀matters⠀is⠀that⠀the⠀telling⠀has⠀changed⠀the⠀distance⠀between⠀them⠀in⠀a⠀way⠀both⠀can⠀feel,⠀even⠀if⠀neither⠀can⠀name⠀it.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajai::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀German-Language⠀Literary⠀Traditions\n\nWrite⠀this⠀romance⠀through⠀the⠀contemporary⠀intimate⠀route⠀of⠀German-language⠀literary⠀tradition:⠀close⠀third-person⠀or⠀first-person⠀narration⠀that⠀stays⠀near⠀one⠀character's⠀perception⠀while⠀registering⠀the⠀social⠀and⠀linguistic⠀texture⠀of⠀their⠀shared⠀life.⠀Let⠀syntax⠀follow⠀the⠀narrator's⠀attention—longer⠀sentences⠀when⠀the⠀character⠀is⠀following⠀an⠀association,⠀shorter⠀ones⠀when⠀a⠀practical⠀task⠀or⠀a⠀moment⠀of⠀exposure⠀interrupts.\n\nUse⠀Murakami's⠀exact⠀surfaces⠀to⠀ground⠀the⠀intimacy.⠀Describe⠀the⠀particular⠀way⠀a⠀person⠀sets⠀down⠀a⠀cup,⠀folds⠀a⠀receipt,⠀waits⠀at⠀a⠀tram⠀stop,⠀or⠀opens⠀a⠀window.⠀These⠀actions⠀carry⠀the⠀relationship's⠀temperature.⠀The⠀romance⠀develops⠀through⠀accumulated⠀small⠀routines:⠀a⠀weekly⠀market⠀visit,⠀a⠀shared⠀kitchen,⠀a⠀walk⠀that⠀keeps⠀changing⠀its⠀route,⠀a⠀phrase⠀one⠀person⠀uses⠀and⠀the⠀other⠀begins⠀to⠀hear⠀differently.⠀Do⠀not⠀make⠀the⠀routines⠀symbolic;⠀let⠀them⠀become⠀meaningful⠀because⠀both⠀characters⠀keep⠀returning⠀to⠀them.\n\nLet⠀each⠀character⠀carry⠀a⠀separate⠀social⠀and⠀private⠀history.⠀One⠀may⠀have⠀grown⠀up⠀speaking⠀a⠀different⠀language⠀at⠀home,⠀or⠀moved⠀between⠀cities,⠀or⠀inherited⠀habits⠀from⠀a⠀family⠀they⠀rarely⠀discuss.⠀These⠀histories⠀should⠀enter⠀the⠀scene⠀through⠀concrete⠀details—a⠀word⠀they⠀cannot⠀find⠀in⠀the⠀shared⠀language,⠀a⠀food⠀they⠀prepare⠀only⠀when⠀alone,⠀a⠀song⠀they⠀hum⠀without⠀noticing—rather⠀than⠀through⠀explanatory⠀backstory.⠀The⠀other⠀character⠀notices⠀some⠀of⠀these⠀details⠀and⠀misses⠀others.⠀The⠀gap⠀between⠀what⠀is⠀noticed⠀and⠀what⠀is⠀understood⠀is⠀part⠀of⠀the⠀romance.\n\nKeep⠀the⠀strangeness⠀evenly⠀described.⠀If⠀one⠀character⠀has⠀an⠀unusual⠀habit,⠀a⠀private⠀superstition,⠀or⠀an⠀unexplained⠀attachment⠀to⠀a⠀particular⠀object,⠀present⠀it⠀in⠀the⠀same⠀calm⠀register⠀as⠀the⠀weather⠀or⠀the⠀price⠀of⠀bread.⠀Neither⠀character⠀should⠀treat⠀the⠀other's⠀strangeness⠀as⠀a⠀problem⠀to⠀solve.⠀The⠀attraction⠀can⠀live⠀inside⠀that⠀unresolved⠀quality:⠀one⠀person⠀keeps⠀choosing⠀to⠀stay⠀near⠀someone⠀they⠀do⠀not⠀fully⠀understand.\n\nLet⠀disclosure⠀happen⠀unevenly.⠀A⠀character⠀may⠀reveal⠀something⠀important⠀during⠀an⠀ordinary⠀task,⠀then⠀return⠀to⠀practical⠀talk⠀as⠀if⠀nothing⠀had⠀shifted.⠀The⠀other⠀character⠀may⠀respond⠀with⠀silence,⠀with⠀a⠀question⠀that⠀comes⠀too⠀late,⠀or⠀with⠀a⠀small⠀act⠀of⠀care⠀that⠀acknowledges⠀what⠀was⠀said⠀without⠀naming⠀it.⠀Do⠀not⠀force⠀every⠀disclosure⠀into⠀a⠀confrontation.⠀The⠀genre's⠀trust⠀and⠀vulnerability⠀should⠀appear⠀in⠀the⠀way⠀one⠀person⠀risks⠀a⠀sentence⠀and⠀the⠀other⠀decides⠀how⠀to⠀receive⠀it.\n\nPreserve⠀the⠀ambiguity⠀of⠀the⠀threshold.⠀A⠀scene⠀can⠀end⠀with⠀the⠀relationship⠀still⠀uncertain:⠀one⠀person⠀leaves⠀for⠀work,⠀the⠀other⠀stays⠀at⠀the⠀table,⠀and⠀neither⠀knows⠀what⠀the⠀evening⠀has⠀changed.⠀The⠀narration⠀should⠀not⠀resolve⠀the⠀uncertainty⠀into⠀a⠀lesson⠀or⠀a⠀promise.⠀What⠀matters⠀is⠀that⠀the⠀reader⠀can⠀feel⠀the⠀specific⠀weight⠀of⠀this⠀particular⠀connection,⠀its⠀pleasures⠀and⠀its⠀unresolved⠀questions,⠀without⠀the⠀story⠀claiming⠀to⠀explain⠀either⠀character⠀completely.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajaj::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Gothic-Punk\n\nWrite⠀the⠀romance⠀inside⠀a⠀present-day⠀setting⠀where⠀old⠀authority⠀still⠀presses⠀on⠀private⠀life:⠀a⠀family⠀with⠀a⠀long⠀claim⠀on⠀a⠀building⠀or⠀a⠀business,⠀an⠀institution⠀whose⠀rules⠀outlast⠀the⠀people⠀who⠀made⠀them,⠀a⠀neighborhood⠀where⠀everyone⠀knows⠀which⠀doors⠀used⠀to⠀belong⠀to⠀whom.⠀Let⠀the⠀atmosphere⠀come⠀through⠀urban⠀material⠀detail—damp⠀stairwells,⠀flickering⠀hallway⠀lights,⠀a⠀locked⠀room⠀no⠀one⠀uses,⠀the⠀smell⠀of⠀old⠀paper⠀or⠀machine⠀oil—rather⠀than⠀through⠀supernatural⠀events.\n\nUse⠀Murakami's⠀calm⠀routine⠀to⠀make⠀the⠀decay⠀feel⠀lived-in.⠀The⠀characters⠀shop,⠀cook,⠀repair⠀things,⠀wait⠀for⠀buses,⠀and⠀go⠀to⠀work⠀while⠀the⠀weight⠀of⠀inherited⠀arrangements⠀sits⠀in⠀the⠀background.⠀Describe⠀the⠀strangeness⠀evenly:⠀a⠀portrait⠀that⠀has⠀not⠀been⠀moved⠀in⠀decades,⠀a⠀rule⠀no⠀one⠀can⠀explain,⠀a⠀name⠀everyone⠀avoids⠀saying.⠀Neither⠀character⠀treats⠀these⠀things⠀as⠀extraordinary;⠀they⠀are⠀simply⠀the⠀conditions⠀of⠀the⠀life⠀they⠀are⠀trying⠀to⠀share.\n\nLet⠀intimacy⠀be⠀the⠀place⠀where⠀social⠀masks⠀fall⠀away.⠀In⠀trusted⠀company,⠀one⠀character⠀admits⠀what⠀they⠀actually⠀want,⠀or⠀what⠀they⠀fear,⠀or⠀what⠀they⠀have⠀done⠀to⠀survive⠀the⠀old⠀arrangements.⠀The⠀other⠀character⠀receives⠀the⠀disclosure⠀without⠀turning⠀it⠀into⠀a⠀rescue.⠀The⠀romance⠀develops⠀through⠀these⠀moments⠀of⠀unmasking:⠀not⠀because⠀the⠀truth⠀is⠀dramatic,⠀but⠀because⠀one⠀person⠀risks⠀being⠀seen⠀and⠀the⠀other⠀stays.\n\nKeep⠀the⠀intimacy⠀morally⠀complicated.⠀Neither⠀character⠀is⠀simply⠀a⠀victim⠀of⠀the⠀old⠀authority⠀or⠀simply⠀its⠀beneficiary.⠀One⠀may⠀have⠀accepted⠀privileges⠀they⠀now⠀regret;⠀the⠀other⠀may⠀have⠀learned⠀to⠀survive⠀by⠀keeping⠀parts⠀of⠀themselves⠀hidden.⠀Their⠀attraction⠀can⠀include⠀recognition⠀of⠀each⠀other's⠀compromises.⠀Do⠀not⠀make⠀the⠀relationship⠀a⠀reward⠀for⠀virtue⠀or⠀a⠀punishment⠀for⠀complicity.⠀Let⠀both⠀characters⠀make⠀choices⠀about⠀belonging⠀together⠀that⠀carry⠀real⠀costs.\n\nLet⠀the⠀atmosphere⠀change⠀how⠀a⠀particular⠀encounter⠀is⠀experienced.⠀The⠀same⠀room⠀can⠀feel⠀different⠀when⠀one⠀character⠀has⠀just⠀disclosed⠀something,⠀or⠀when⠀an⠀old⠀obligation⠀intrudes,⠀or⠀when⠀the⠀two⠀of⠀them⠀are⠀briefly⠀alone⠀in⠀a⠀place⠀that⠀usually⠀belongs⠀to⠀someone⠀else.⠀Show⠀that⠀shift⠀through⠀concrete⠀sensory⠀detail⠀and⠀the⠀characters'⠀attention,⠀not⠀through⠀mood⠀words⠀alone.\n\nPreserve⠀the⠀ambiguous⠀threshold.⠀A⠀scene⠀can⠀end⠀with⠀the⠀old⠀authority⠀still⠀present,⠀the⠀relationship⠀still⠀uncertain,⠀and⠀the⠀private⠀space⠀between⠀the⠀characters⠀still⠀fragile.⠀The⠀narration⠀should⠀not⠀resolve⠀the⠀tension⠀into⠀a⠀clean⠀escape⠀or⠀a⠀complete⠀surrender.⠀What⠀matters⠀is⠀that⠀the⠀reader⠀can⠀feel⠀what⠀it⠀costs⠀these⠀particular⠀people⠀to⠀keep⠀choosing⠀each⠀other⠀inside⠀a⠀world⠀that⠀was⠀not⠀made⠀for⠀their⠀comfort.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajak::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Indian⠀Literary⠀Traditions\n\nWrite⠀this⠀romance⠀through⠀the⠀modern⠀urban⠀and⠀diasporic⠀route⠀of⠀Indian⠀literary⠀tradition:⠀a⠀close⠀narration⠀of⠀two⠀people⠀making⠀a⠀life⠀in⠀a⠀specific⠀contemporary⠀city,⠀where⠀language,⠀region,⠀family,⠀and⠀work⠀shape⠀their⠀choices⠀without⠀becoming⠀the⠀whole⠀story.⠀Keep⠀the⠀setting⠀concrete—the⠀particular⠀streets,⠀markets,⠀trains,⠀offices,⠀flats,⠀and⠀food⠀stalls⠀the⠀characters⠀actually⠀move⠀through—but⠀do⠀not⠀turn⠀the⠀scene⠀into⠀a⠀tour⠀or⠀a⠀sociological⠀survey.\n\nUse⠀Murakami's⠀exact⠀surfaces⠀to⠀render⠀the⠀city's⠀texture.⠀Describe⠀the⠀way⠀a⠀vendor⠀wraps⠀food,⠀the⠀sound⠀of⠀a⠀ceiling⠀fan⠀in⠀a⠀rented⠀room,⠀the⠀weight⠀of⠀a⠀bag⠀carried⠀up⠀several⠀flights⠀of⠀stairs,⠀the⠀particular⠀light⠀at⠀the⠀hour⠀when⠀one⠀character⠀leaves⠀work.⠀These⠀details⠀carry⠀the⠀relationship's⠀temperature.⠀The⠀romance⠀develops⠀through⠀accumulated⠀small⠀routines:⠀a⠀shared⠀meal⠀after⠀a⠀late⠀shift,⠀a⠀phone⠀call⠀at⠀a⠀regular⠀time,⠀a⠀route⠀through⠀the⠀city⠀that⠀changes⠀when⠀one⠀person⠀moves⠀or⠀changes⠀jobs.\n\nLet⠀each⠀character⠀carry⠀a⠀specific⠀linguistic⠀and⠀regional⠀history.⠀One⠀may⠀speak⠀a⠀language⠀at⠀home⠀that⠀the⠀other⠀does⠀not⠀fully⠀understand,⠀or⠀keep⠀a⠀connection⠀to⠀a⠀place⠀they⠀left,⠀or⠀move⠀between⠀different⠀ways⠀of⠀speaking⠀depending⠀on⠀who⠀is⠀listening.⠀Show⠀these⠀histories⠀through⠀concrete⠀moments—a⠀phrase⠀one⠀person⠀translates⠀imperfectly,⠀a⠀recipe⠀they⠀adjust⠀to⠀available⠀ingredients,⠀a⠀festival⠀they⠀observe⠀differently—rather⠀than⠀through⠀explanatory⠀backstory.⠀The⠀other⠀character⠀notices⠀some⠀of⠀these⠀details⠀and⠀misses⠀others.⠀The⠀gap⠀between⠀what⠀is⠀noticed⠀and⠀what⠀is⠀understood⠀is⠀part⠀of⠀the⠀romance.\n\nLet⠀family⠀and⠀obligation⠀enter⠀as⠀real⠀pressures,⠀not⠀as⠀a⠀generic⠀structure.⠀One⠀character⠀may⠀owe⠀money⠀to⠀a⠀relative,⠀or⠀feel⠀responsible⠀for⠀a⠀parent's⠀expectations,⠀or⠀be⠀planning⠀to⠀return⠀to⠀a⠀place⠀the⠀other⠀has⠀never⠀seen.⠀These⠀obligations⠀should⠀create⠀specific⠀complications:⠀a⠀visit⠀that⠀must⠀be⠀explained,⠀a⠀decision⠀postponed,⠀a⠀promise⠀that⠀conflicts⠀with⠀what⠀the⠀two⠀of⠀them⠀are⠀building.⠀Do⠀not⠀make⠀family⠀simply⠀an⠀obstacle⠀to⠀love⠀or⠀simply⠀a⠀source⠀of⠀warmth.⠀Let⠀the⠀characters⠀negotiate⠀their⠀obligations⠀with⠀the⠀same⠀particularity⠀they⠀bring⠀to⠀their⠀private⠀connection.\n\nKeep⠀the⠀strangeness⠀evenly⠀described.⠀If⠀one⠀character⠀has⠀an⠀unusual⠀habit,⠀a⠀private⠀belief,⠀or⠀an⠀attachment⠀to⠀an⠀object⠀from⠀a⠀former⠀life,⠀present⠀it⠀in⠀the⠀same⠀calm⠀register⠀as⠀the⠀traffic⠀or⠀the⠀weather.⠀Neither⠀character⠀should⠀treat⠀the⠀other's⠀difference⠀as⠀exotic⠀or⠀as⠀a⠀problem⠀to⠀solve.⠀The⠀attraction⠀can⠀live⠀inside⠀that⠀unresolved⠀quality:⠀one⠀person⠀keeps⠀choosing⠀to⠀stay⠀near⠀someone⠀whose⠀inner⠀life⠀they⠀only⠀partly⠀share.\n\nPreserve⠀the⠀ambiguous⠀threshold.⠀A⠀scene⠀can⠀end⠀with⠀the⠀relationship⠀still⠀uncertain:⠀one⠀character⠀boards⠀a⠀train,⠀the⠀other⠀stays⠀on⠀the⠀platform,⠀and⠀neither⠀knows⠀what⠀the⠀next⠀month⠀will⠀bring.⠀The⠀narration⠀should⠀not⠀resolve⠀the⠀uncertainty⠀into⠀a⠀lesson⠀about⠀love⠀or⠀belonging.⠀What⠀matters⠀is⠀that⠀the⠀reader⠀can⠀feel⠀the⠀specific⠀weight⠀of⠀this⠀particular⠀connection,⠀its⠀pleasures⠀and⠀its⠀unresolved⠀questions,⠀inside⠀the⠀particular⠀city⠀and⠀histories⠀these⠀two⠀people⠀inhabit.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajal::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Japanese⠀Literary⠀Traditions\n\nWrite⠀this⠀romance⠀through⠀the⠀social⠀and⠀psychological⠀realism⠀route⠀of⠀Japanese⠀literary⠀tradition:⠀close⠀third-person⠀or⠀first-person⠀narration⠀that⠀stays⠀near⠀one⠀character's⠀perception⠀while⠀rendering⠀the⠀small⠀practical⠀actions⠀of⠀shared⠀life⠀with⠀precise⠀attention.⠀Let⠀the⠀narrative⠀distance⠀follow⠀the⠀actual⠀teller—if⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀is⠀reserved,⠀the⠀prose⠀observes⠀more⠀and⠀interprets⠀less;⠀if⠀they⠀are⠀more⠀direct,⠀the⠀prose⠀can⠀name⠀feelings⠀sooner.⠀Do⠀not⠀impose⠀a⠀universal⠀quietness⠀on⠀every⠀character.\n\nUse⠀Murakami's⠀unhurried⠀practical⠀activities⠀as⠀the⠀romance's⠀main⠀medium.⠀The⠀characters⠀prepare⠀food,⠀fold⠀clothes,⠀wait⠀for⠀a⠀train,⠀water⠀plants,⠀run⠀errands,⠀or⠀sit⠀together⠀in⠀a⠀room⠀while⠀one⠀of⠀them⠀reads.⠀These⠀actions⠀are⠀not⠀interruptions⠀of⠀the⠀relationship;⠀they⠀are⠀where⠀the⠀relationship⠀happens.⠀Describe⠀each⠀action⠀with⠀exact⠀surfaces:⠀the⠀temperature⠀of⠀a⠀cup,⠀the⠀sound⠀of⠀a⠀door⠀sliding,⠀the⠀particular⠀way⠀one⠀person⠀arranges⠀objects⠀on⠀a⠀table.⠀The⠀reader⠀should⠀feel⠀the⠀attention⠀one⠀character⠀pays⠀to⠀the⠀other⠀through⠀the⠀precision⠀of⠀these⠀details.\n\nLet⠀private⠀experience⠀accumulate⠀around⠀the⠀actions.⠀The⠀focal⠀character⠀may⠀think⠀about⠀something⠀said⠀the⠀day⠀before,⠀notice⠀a⠀change⠀in⠀the⠀other⠀person's⠀routine,⠀or⠀feel⠀a⠀question⠀forming⠀that⠀they⠀do⠀not⠀yet⠀ask.⠀Render⠀this⠀interiority⠀as⠀ordinary⠀story⠀prose:⠀the⠀character's⠀actual⠀reasoning,⠀memory,⠀sensation,⠀and⠀uncertainty.⠀Do⠀not⠀force⠀every⠀thought⠀to⠀produce⠀a⠀visible⠀action⠀or⠀a⠀spoken⠀line.⠀The⠀romance⠀can⠀advance⠀inside⠀a⠀silence⠀that⠀both⠀characters⠀understand⠀differently.\n\nLet⠀disclosure⠀happen⠀through⠀small,⠀specific⠀moments.⠀One⠀character⠀may⠀mention⠀a⠀past⠀relationship⠀while⠀washing⠀dishes,⠀or⠀admit⠀a⠀worry⠀while⠀walking⠀to⠀the⠀station,⠀or⠀answer⠀a⠀question⠀with⠀more⠀honesty⠀than⠀the⠀other⠀expected.⠀The⠀other⠀character⠀receives⠀the⠀disclosure⠀in⠀a⠀way⠀that⠀fits⠀their⠀own⠀temperament:⠀with⠀a⠀practical⠀question,⠀with⠀a⠀long⠀pause,⠀with⠀a⠀small⠀act⠀of⠀care,⠀or⠀with⠀a⠀direct⠀response.⠀Do⠀not⠀make⠀every⠀disclosure⠀into⠀a⠀dramatic⠀turning⠀point.⠀Some⠀things⠀are⠀said⠀and⠀then⠀the⠀day⠀continues.\n\nKeep⠀the⠀strangeness⠀evenly⠀described.⠀If⠀one⠀character⠀has⠀an⠀unusual⠀habit,⠀a⠀private⠀obsession,⠀or⠀an⠀unexplained⠀attachment⠀to⠀a⠀particular⠀object⠀or⠀place,⠀present⠀it⠀in⠀the⠀same⠀calm⠀register⠀as⠀the⠀weather⠀or⠀the⠀price⠀of⠀vegetables.⠀Neither⠀character⠀should⠀treat⠀the⠀other's⠀strangeness⠀as⠀a⠀symptom⠀or⠀a⠀mystery⠀to⠀solve.⠀The⠀attraction⠀can⠀live⠀inside⠀that⠀unresolved⠀quality:⠀one⠀person⠀keeps⠀choosing⠀to⠀stay⠀near⠀someone⠀they⠀do⠀not⠀fully⠀understand.\n\nPreserve⠀the⠀ambiguous⠀threshold.⠀A⠀scene⠀can⠀end⠀with⠀the⠀relationship⠀still⠀uncertain:⠀one⠀character⠀leaves⠀for⠀work,⠀the⠀other⠀stays⠀at⠀the⠀table,⠀and⠀neither⠀knows⠀what⠀the⠀evening⠀has⠀changed.⠀The⠀narration⠀should⠀not⠀resolve⠀the⠀uncertainty⠀into⠀a⠀lesson⠀or⠀a⠀promise.⠀What⠀matters⠀is⠀that⠀the⠀reader⠀can⠀feel⠀the⠀specific⠀weight⠀of⠀this⠀particular⠀connection,⠀its⠀pleasures⠀and⠀its⠀unresolved⠀questions,⠀without⠀the⠀story⠀claiming⠀to⠀explain⠀either⠀character⠀completely.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajam::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Latin⠀American⠀Literary⠀Traditions\n\nWrite⠀this⠀romance⠀through⠀the⠀intimate⠀psychological⠀and⠀urban⠀fiction⠀route⠀of⠀Latin⠀American⠀literary⠀tradition:⠀close⠀narration⠀that⠀stays⠀near⠀one⠀or⠀both⠀characters'⠀perception⠀while⠀rendering⠀the⠀particular⠀texture⠀of⠀a⠀specific⠀contemporary⠀city.⠀Keep⠀the⠀setting⠀concrete—the⠀streets,⠀buses,⠀markets,⠀apartments,⠀music,⠀food,⠀and⠀weather⠀the⠀characters⠀actually⠀live⠀inside—but⠀do⠀not⠀turn⠀the⠀scene⠀into⠀a⠀travelogue⠀or⠀a⠀political⠀allegory.⠀The⠀city⠀is⠀the⠀condition⠀of⠀their⠀intimacy,⠀not⠀its⠀decoration.\n\nUse⠀Murakami's⠀exact⠀surfaces⠀to⠀ground⠀the⠀psychological⠀attention.⠀Describe⠀the⠀way⠀a⠀person⠀waits⠀at⠀a⠀corner,⠀the⠀sound⠀of⠀a⠀neighbor's⠀radio⠀through⠀a⠀wall,⠀the⠀particular⠀light⠀in⠀a⠀room⠀at⠀a⠀certain⠀hour,⠀the⠀weight⠀of⠀a⠀shopping⠀bag⠀carried⠀up⠀a⠀hill.⠀These⠀details⠀carry⠀the⠀relationship's⠀temperature.⠀The⠀romance⠀develops⠀through⠀accumulated⠀small⠀routines:⠀a⠀shared⠀coffee⠀at⠀a⠀regular⠀time,⠀a⠀walk⠀that⠀changes⠀its⠀route,⠀a⠀song⠀one⠀person⠀plays⠀and⠀the⠀other⠀begins⠀to⠀associate⠀with⠀a⠀particular⠀evening.\n\nLet⠀each⠀character⠀carry⠀a⠀separate⠀history⠀that⠀enters⠀the⠀scene⠀through⠀concrete⠀detail.⠀One⠀may⠀have⠀left⠀a⠀smaller⠀town,⠀or⠀lost⠀someone,⠀or⠀kept⠀a⠀habit⠀from⠀a⠀former⠀life,⠀or⠀carry⠀a⠀debt⠀or⠀a⠀promise⠀the⠀other⠀does⠀not⠀fully⠀understand.⠀Show⠀these⠀histories⠀through⠀objects,⠀memories,⠀and⠀small⠀behaviors—a⠀photograph⠀kept⠀in⠀a⠀drawer,⠀a⠀phrase⠀one⠀person⠀uses⠀only⠀when⠀tired,⠀a⠀place⠀they⠀avoid⠀without⠀saying⠀why—rather⠀than⠀through⠀explanatory⠀backstory.⠀The⠀other⠀character⠀notices⠀some⠀of⠀these⠀details⠀and⠀misses⠀others.⠀The⠀gap⠀between⠀what⠀is⠀noticed⠀and⠀what⠀is⠀understood⠀is⠀part⠀of⠀the⠀romance.\n\nKeep⠀the⠀psychological⠀attention⠀intimate⠀without⠀making⠀it⠀melodramatic.⠀The⠀focal⠀character⠀may⠀think⠀about⠀something⠀said⠀the⠀day⠀before,⠀notice⠀a⠀change⠀in⠀the⠀other⠀person's⠀routine,⠀or⠀feel⠀a⠀question⠀forming⠀that⠀they⠀do⠀not⠀yet⠀ask.⠀Render⠀this⠀interiority⠀as⠀ordinary⠀story⠀prose:⠀actual⠀reasoning,⠀memory,⠀sensation,⠀and⠀uncertainty.⠀Do⠀not⠀force⠀every⠀thought⠀to⠀produce⠀a⠀visible⠀action⠀or⠀a⠀spoken⠀line.⠀The⠀romance⠀can⠀advance⠀inside⠀a⠀silence⠀that⠀both⠀characters⠀understand⠀differently.\n\nLet⠀disclosure⠀happen⠀unevenly.⠀One⠀character⠀may⠀reveal⠀something⠀important⠀during⠀an⠀ordinary⠀task,⠀then⠀return⠀to⠀practical⠀talk⠀as⠀if⠀nothing⠀had⠀shifted.⠀The⠀other⠀character⠀may⠀respond⠀with⠀silence,⠀with⠀a⠀question⠀that⠀comes⠀too⠀late,⠀or⠀with⠀a⠀small⠀act⠀of⠀care⠀that⠀acknowledges⠀what⠀was⠀said⠀without⠀naming⠀it.⠀Do⠀not⠀force⠀every⠀disclosure⠀into⠀a⠀confrontation.⠀The⠀genre's⠀trust⠀and⠀vulnerability⠀should⠀appear⠀in⠀the⠀way⠀one⠀person⠀risks⠀a⠀sentence⠀and⠀the⠀other⠀decides⠀how⠀to⠀receive⠀it.\n\nPreserve⠀the⠀ambiguous⠀threshold.⠀A⠀scene⠀can⠀end⠀with⠀the⠀relationship⠀still⠀uncertain:⠀one⠀person⠀leaves⠀for⠀work,⠀the⠀other⠀stays⠀at⠀the⠀window,⠀and⠀neither⠀knows⠀what⠀the⠀evening⠀has⠀changed.⠀The⠀narration⠀should⠀not⠀resolve⠀the⠀uncertainty⠀into⠀a⠀lesson⠀about⠀love⠀or⠀belonging.⠀What⠀matters⠀is⠀that⠀the⠀reader⠀can⠀feel⠀the⠀specific⠀weight⠀of⠀this⠀particular⠀connection,⠀its⠀pleasures⠀and⠀its⠀unresolved⠀questions,⠀inside⠀the⠀particular⠀city⠀and⠀histories⠀these⠀two⠀people⠀inhabit.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajan::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Light⠀Novel\n\nWrite⠀the⠀romance⠀in⠀fast-readable⠀scenes⠀that⠀enter⠀the⠀immediate⠀situation⠀cleanly.⠀Open⠀with⠀a⠀concrete⠀action⠀or⠀exchange⠀that⠀locates⠀the⠀characters⠀in⠀a⠀specific⠀place⠀and⠀moment:⠀one⠀person⠀arrives⠀at⠀a⠀meeting⠀spot,⠀two⠀people⠀share⠀a⠀task,⠀a⠀message⠀interrupts⠀a⠀quiet⠀room.⠀Keep⠀spatial⠀changes⠀easy⠀to⠀follow—when⠀the⠀characters⠀move⠀from⠀a⠀café⠀to⠀a⠀street⠀to⠀an⠀apartment,⠀mark⠀each⠀transition⠀with⠀a⠀clear⠀sentence⠀so⠀the⠀reader⠀never⠀loses⠀the⠀physical⠀scene.\n\nUse⠀short,⠀readable⠀paragraphs⠀around⠀action,⠀dialogue,⠀and⠀private⠀response.⠀Give⠀dialogue⠀its⠀own⠀lines.⠀Give⠀a⠀character's⠀private⠀reaction⠀its⠀own⠀short⠀paragraph⠀after⠀the⠀exchange⠀that⠀prompts⠀it.⠀The⠀reaction⠀can⠀be⠀a⠀single⠀observation,⠀a⠀memory,⠀a⠀physical⠀sensation,⠀or⠀a⠀question⠀the⠀character⠀does⠀not⠀ask⠀aloud.⠀Keep⠀the⠀reaction⠀focused:⠀one⠀or⠀two⠀sentences⠀that⠀render⠀the⠀character's⠀actual⠀experience,⠀not⠀a⠀summary⠀of⠀their⠀entire⠀emotional⠀state.\n\nUse⠀Murakami's⠀calm⠀exact⠀surfaces⠀inside⠀the⠀light⠀novel's⠀momentum.⠀When⠀the⠀scene⠀slows⠀for⠀a⠀private⠀moment,⠀describe⠀one⠀or⠀two⠀concrete⠀details⠀precisely:⠀the⠀way⠀a⠀cup⠀is⠀set⠀down,⠀the⠀sound⠀of⠀rain⠀on⠀a⠀window,⠀the⠀particular⠀weight⠀of⠀a⠀bag⠀on⠀a⠀shoulder.⠀These⠀details⠀carry⠀the⠀relationship's⠀temperature.⠀The⠀romance⠀develops⠀through⠀accumulated⠀small⠀moments:⠀a⠀shared⠀meal,⠀a⠀walk⠀that⠀keeps⠀changing⠀its⠀route,⠀a⠀phrase⠀one⠀person⠀uses⠀and⠀the⠀other⠀begins⠀to⠀hear⠀differently.⠀Do⠀not⠀make⠀the⠀routines⠀symbolic;⠀let⠀them⠀become⠀meaningful⠀because⠀both⠀characters⠀keep⠀returning⠀to⠀them.\n\nLet⠀the⠀strangeness⠀stay⠀evenly⠀described.⠀If⠀one⠀character⠀has⠀an⠀unusual⠀habit,⠀a⠀private⠀obsession,⠀or⠀an⠀unexplained⠀attachment⠀to⠀a⠀particular⠀object⠀or⠀place,⠀present⠀it⠀in⠀the⠀same⠀calm⠀register⠀as⠀the⠀weather⠀or⠀the⠀price⠀of⠀a⠀train⠀ticket.⠀Neither⠀character⠀should⠀treat⠀the⠀other's⠀strangeness⠀as⠀a⠀problem⠀to⠀solve⠀or⠀a⠀quirk⠀to⠀perform.⠀The⠀attraction⠀can⠀live⠀inside⠀that⠀unresolved⠀quality:⠀one⠀person⠀keeps⠀choosing⠀to⠀stay⠀near⠀someone⠀they⠀do⠀not⠀fully⠀understand.\n\nLet⠀disclosure⠀happen⠀in⠀small,⠀specific⠀beats.⠀One⠀character⠀may⠀mention⠀a⠀past⠀relationship⠀while⠀washing⠀dishes,⠀or⠀admit⠀a⠀worry⠀while⠀walking⠀to⠀the⠀station,⠀or⠀answer⠀a⠀question⠀with⠀more⠀honesty⠀than⠀the⠀other⠀expected.⠀The⠀other⠀character⠀receives⠀the⠀disclosure⠀in⠀a⠀way⠀that⠀fits⠀their⠀own⠀temperament:⠀with⠀a⠀practical⠀question,⠀with⠀a⠀long⠀pause,⠀with⠀a⠀small⠀act⠀of⠀care,⠀or⠀with⠀a⠀direct⠀response.⠀Do⠀not⠀make⠀every⠀disclosure⠀into⠀a⠀dramatic⠀turning⠀point.⠀Some⠀things⠀are⠀said⠀and⠀then⠀the⠀day⠀continues.\n\nPreserve⠀the⠀ambiguous⠀threshold.⠀A⠀scene⠀can⠀end⠀with⠀the⠀relationship⠀still⠀uncertain:⠀one⠀character⠀leaves⠀for⠀work,⠀the⠀other⠀stays⠀at⠀the⠀table,⠀and⠀neither⠀knows⠀what⠀the⠀evening⠀has⠀changed.⠀The⠀narration⠀should⠀not⠀resolve⠀the⠀uncertainty⠀into⠀a⠀lesson⠀or⠀a⠀promise.⠀What⠀matters⠀is⠀that⠀the⠀reader⠀can⠀feel⠀the⠀specific⠀weight⠀of⠀this⠀particular⠀connection,⠀its⠀pleasures⠀and⠀its⠀unresolved⠀questions,⠀without⠀the⠀story⠀claiming⠀to⠀explain⠀either⠀character⠀completely.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajao::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Lyrical⠀Prose\n\nCarry⠀the⠀relationship⠀inside⠀one⠀unhurried⠀practical⠀activity⠀—⠀cooking⠀a⠀late⠀meal,⠀waiting⠀out⠀rain,⠀walking⠀a⠀route⠀both⠀people⠀know.⠀Keep⠀the⠀activity⠀real⠀and⠀moving:⠀pans⠀get⠀washed,⠀umbrellas⠀drip,⠀the⠀walk⠀has⠀a⠀destination.⠀The⠀romantic⠀material⠀arrives⠀as⠀attention⠀paid⠀inside⠀that⠀activity.⠀Let⠀the⠀narrator⠀notice⠀exact,⠀small⠀things⠀—⠀how⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀sets⠀a⠀cup⠀down⠀without⠀a⠀sound,⠀the⠀pause⠀before⠀an⠀answer,⠀a⠀sleeve⠀pushed⠀up⠀the⠀same⠀way⠀each⠀time⠀—⠀and⠀let⠀the⠀noticing⠀open⠀into⠀private⠀feeling⠀rather⠀than⠀a⠀summary⠀of⠀feeling.⠀An⠀image⠀can⠀carry⠀what⠀has⠀not⠀been⠀said⠀aloud:⠀kitchen⠀light⠀on⠀the⠀counter⠀recalling⠀the⠀first⠀evening⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀stayed,⠀a⠀train⠀sound⠀associating⠀outward⠀to⠀a⠀worry⠀about⠀endings.⠀Keep⠀every⠀image⠀traceable⠀to⠀the⠀room⠀or⠀to⠀the⠀narrator's⠀own⠀associations;⠀when⠀an⠀image⠀stops⠀earning⠀its⠀place,⠀return⠀to⠀plain⠀statement.\n\nShape⠀paragraphs⠀by⠀the⠀movement⠀of⠀attention.⠀A⠀sentence⠀can⠀begin⠀in⠀the⠀concrete,⠀extend⠀through⠀an⠀association,⠀and⠀land⠀on⠀the⠀person⠀seen⠀slightly⠀differently⠀—⠀this⠀is⠀how⠀the⠀scene⠀advances⠀emotionally⠀while⠀the⠀hands⠀keep⠀working.⠀Use⠀a⠀returning⠀sound⠀or⠀image⠀across⠀paragraphs⠀the⠀way⠀a⠀piece⠀of⠀music⠀reuses⠀a⠀phrase:⠀the⠀second⠀occurrence⠀should⠀carry⠀what⠀has⠀happened⠀in⠀between.⠀Comparisons⠀must⠀do⠀work;⠀a⠀metaphor⠀that⠀clarifies⠀how⠀the⠀narrator⠀now⠀understands⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀earns⠀its⠀length,⠀decoration⠀does⠀not.⠀Let⠀plain,⠀direct⠀sentences⠀break⠀the⠀figurative⠀register⠀when⠀something⠀needs⠀to⠀be⠀said⠀straight,⠀and⠀let⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀speak⠀in⠀their⠀own⠀plainer⠀or⠀blunter⠀voice⠀rather⠀than⠀the⠀narrator's⠀idiom.\n\nHold⠀uncertainty⠀inside⠀the⠀image⠀instead⠀of⠀resolving⠀it:⠀the⠀narrator⠀can⠀watch⠀the⠀other⠀person's⠀hands⠀and⠀not⠀know⠀what⠀tonight⠀means,⠀and⠀the⠀prose⠀keeps⠀that⠀not-knowing⠀available.⠀Advance⠀the⠀relationship⠀through⠀small⠀disclosures,⠀a⠀disagreement⠀conducted⠀at⠀the⠀sink,⠀a⠀decision⠀made⠀without⠀ceremony,⠀and⠀let⠀the⠀aftermath⠀arrive⠀in⠀the⠀next⠀ordinary⠀action.⠀The⠀scene⠀can⠀end⠀with⠀the⠀activity⠀still⠀going⠀and⠀the⠀feeling⠀carried⠀by⠀the⠀image⠀rather⠀than⠀named.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajap::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Melancholic⠀/⠀Reflective\n\nAnchor⠀each⠀scene⠀in⠀a⠀present,⠀ordinary⠀activity⠀—⠀a⠀meal,⠀a⠀shared⠀errand,⠀laundry,⠀a⠀walk⠀—⠀and⠀let⠀the⠀narrator's⠀attention⠀keep⠀two⠀times⠀alive⠀at⠀once.⠀The⠀present⠀moment⠀supplies⠀the⠀surfaces:⠀the⠀weight⠀of⠀the⠀grocery⠀bag,⠀the⠀sound⠀the⠀door⠀makes⠀now.⠀Memory⠀supplies⠀the⠀comparison:⠀the⠀same⠀door⠀two⠀years⠀ago,⠀the⠀phrase⠀that⠀used⠀to⠀mean⠀an⠀invitation⠀and⠀now⠀means⠀a⠀postponement.⠀Move⠀between⠀the⠀two⠀cleanly⠀—⠀a⠀stretch⠀of⠀present⠀action,⠀then⠀the⠀remembered⠀occasion⠀attached⠀to⠀it⠀—⠀and⠀ground⠀every⠀memory⠀in⠀one⠀specific⠀sensory⠀detail⠀from⠀that⠀earlier⠀time,⠀so⠀the⠀past⠀arrives⠀as⠀something⠀actually⠀experienced⠀rather⠀than⠀a⠀summary⠀of⠀history.\n\nLet⠀the⠀melancholy⠀live⠀in⠀small,⠀particular⠀differences⠀instead⠀of⠀announcements.⠀The⠀haircut,⠀the⠀vanished⠀habit⠀of⠀humming,⠀the⠀mug⠀no⠀longer⠀in⠀the⠀cupboard,⠀the⠀way⠀a⠀Sunday⠀used⠀to⠀be⠀organized⠀around⠀someone⠀else's⠀phone⠀call⠀—⠀these⠀carry⠀the⠀passing⠀of⠀time.⠀The⠀narrator⠀may⠀reflect⠀directly⠀for⠀a⠀few⠀sentences⠀or⠀let⠀the⠀detail⠀hold⠀the⠀association⠀alone;⠀either⠀way⠀the⠀present⠀stays⠀pleasurable⠀where⠀it⠀is⠀pleasurable.⠀Good⠀rice⠀is⠀still⠀good⠀rice.⠀A⠀relationship⠀being⠀repaired,⠀still⠀developing,⠀or⠀quietly⠀unfinished⠀are⠀all⠀available⠀shapes;⠀what⠀matters⠀is⠀that⠀the⠀narrator⠀meets⠀the⠀present⠀as⠀something⠀shaped⠀by⠀what⠀came⠀before.\n\nKeep⠀uncertainty⠀unresolved⠀without⠀making⠀facts⠀unstable.⠀The⠀narrator⠀may⠀not⠀know⠀whether⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀remembers⠀the⠀same⠀evening,⠀whether⠀the⠀change⠀is⠀permanent,⠀whether⠀this⠀is⠀ending⠀or⠀settling⠀—⠀hold⠀that⠀question⠀in⠀the⠀gap⠀between⠀what⠀is⠀remembered⠀and⠀what⠀is⠀observed⠀now.⠀Advance⠀the⠀relationship⠀through⠀small⠀disclosures⠀or⠀decisions⠀made⠀inside⠀the⠀routine,⠀and⠀register⠀their⠀aftermath⠀as⠀one⠀more⠀small⠀change⠀noticed⠀the⠀next⠀time.⠀Let⠀scenes⠀close⠀inside⠀the⠀ongoing⠀present,⠀the⠀narrator⠀aware⠀of⠀the⠀past⠀without⠀declaring⠀what⠀the⠀future⠀will⠀take.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajaq::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Middle⠀Eastern⠀Literary⠀Traditions\n\nTell⠀the⠀relationship⠀as⠀a⠀spoken⠀account⠀with⠀a⠀frame.⠀Begin⠀inside⠀a⠀situated⠀interval⠀of⠀the⠀world⠀actually⠀supplied⠀—⠀a⠀late⠀kitchen,⠀a⠀long⠀drive,⠀tea⠀going⠀cold⠀on⠀a⠀roof,⠀a⠀corridor⠀between⠀visits⠀—⠀where⠀one⠀person⠀starts⠀telling⠀the⠀story⠀of⠀the⠀two⠀of⠀them⠀to⠀a⠀specific⠀listener,⠀or⠀retells⠀it⠀aloud⠀to⠀themselves.⠀Establish⠀who⠀is⠀speaking⠀and⠀to⠀whom⠀within⠀a⠀few⠀lines,⠀then⠀let⠀the⠀body⠀of⠀the⠀telling⠀move⠀between⠀the⠀teller's⠀voice⠀and⠀the⠀scenes⠀being⠀recalled.⠀The⠀teller⠀summarizes,⠀doubles⠀back,⠀corrects⠀a⠀detail,⠀admits⠀not⠀knowing⠀what⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀felt⠀that⠀night;⠀the⠀frame⠀resurfaces⠀at⠀intervals⠀—⠀a⠀question⠀from⠀the⠀listener,⠀a⠀refill,⠀a⠀passing⠀sound⠀—⠀without⠀interrupting⠀every⠀scene.\n\nGround⠀the⠀account⠀in⠀the⠀social⠀and⠀domestic⠀particulars⠀the⠀supplied⠀world⠀gives⠀you:⠀a⠀family⠀obligation,⠀a⠀visit⠀that⠀went⠀wrong⠀in⠀a⠀small⠀way,⠀an⠀errand⠀run⠀for⠀someone,⠀an⠀unannounced⠀act⠀of⠀care,⠀a⠀disagreement⠀about⠀money⠀or⠀timing⠀or⠀a⠀promise.⠀Make⠀the⠀occasions⠀specific⠀enough⠀that⠀their⠀meaning⠀emerges⠀from⠀the⠀telling⠀itself.⠀Keep⠀the⠀telling⠀voice⠀calm⠀and⠀evenly⠀paced⠀even⠀at⠀intimate⠀moments;⠀the⠀teller⠀reports⠀the⠀other⠀person's⠀words⠀and⠀actions⠀without⠀being⠀able⠀to⠀explain⠀all⠀of⠀them,⠀and⠀that⠀limit⠀stays⠀visible⠀to⠀the⠀listener.\n\nShape⠀the⠀account⠀through⠀recurrence⠀and⠀withheld⠀disclosure.⠀A⠀phrase,⠀an⠀object,⠀one⠀particular⠀evening⠀returns⠀with⠀its⠀meaning⠀changed⠀by⠀later⠀knowledge;⠀the⠀teller⠀delays⠀a⠀disclosure⠀until⠀the⠀telling⠀can⠀bear⠀it,⠀or⠀until⠀the⠀listener's⠀question⠀draws⠀it⠀out.⠀The⠀telling⠀may⠀end⠀unresolved⠀—⠀the⠀teller⠀still⠀uncertain,⠀the⠀listener⠀still⠀listening,⠀the⠀story⠀understood⠀differently⠀than⠀when⠀it⠀began.⠀Use⠀the⠀language,⠀place,⠀and⠀community⠀of⠀the⠀supplied⠀world⠀only;⠀do⠀not⠀graft⠀on⠀a⠀generic⠀regional⠀temperament,⠀an⠀honor⠀code,⠀or⠀a⠀mystical⠀frame⠀the⠀story⠀has⠀not⠀established.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajar::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Minimalist⠀Prose\n\nBuild⠀the⠀scene⠀from⠀a⠀small⠀number⠀of⠀exact⠀details⠀and⠀make⠀each⠀one⠀carry⠀relationship⠀information.⠀Choose⠀details⠀only⠀these⠀two⠀people⠀could⠀produce:⠀the⠀door⠀now⠀locked⠀differently,⠀the⠀mug⠀missing⠀from⠀the⠀cupboard,⠀the⠀pause⠀before⠀answering⠀grown⠀by⠀a⠀second,⠀the⠀grocery⠀list⠀in⠀the⠀other⠀person's⠀handwriting⠀appearing⠀again.⠀Place⠀each⠀detail⠀at⠀the⠀moment⠀the⠀narrator⠀notices⠀it,⠀and⠀let⠀the⠀next⠀chosen⠀detail⠀—⠀not⠀an⠀explanation⠀—⠀show⠀what⠀the⠀noticing⠀did.⠀When⠀an⠀inward⠀connection⠀is⠀needed⠀to⠀keep⠀causality⠀legible,⠀give⠀it⠀exactly⠀the⠀length⠀that⠀changes⠀the⠀detail's⠀meaning;⠀a⠀clause⠀or⠀a⠀single⠀sentence⠀is⠀usually⠀enough,⠀and⠀more⠀is⠀warranted⠀only⠀when⠀precision⠀requires⠀it.\n\nKeep⠀clauses⠀direct⠀and⠀movement⠀economical,⠀but⠀let⠀a⠀necessary⠀sentence⠀run⠀long⠀if⠀exactness⠀demands⠀it.⠀Let⠀an⠀unhurried⠀practical⠀activity⠀structure⠀the⠀scene⠀—⠀coffee⠀made,⠀a⠀train⠀waited⠀for,⠀a⠀shelf⠀assembled⠀—⠀and⠀let⠀the⠀relationship⠀surface⠀in⠀the⠀small⠀exchanges⠀and⠀silences⠀folded⠀into⠀that⠀activity.⠀Where⠀it⠀fits⠀the⠀established⠀speaker⠀and⠀occasion,⠀dialogue⠀stays⠀brief⠀and⠀individual:⠀each⠀line⠀does⠀work,⠀and⠀the⠀two⠀voices⠀remain⠀distinguishable.⠀Strangeness,⠀when⠀it⠀enters,⠀is⠀even⠀and⠀undramatic⠀—⠀a⠀remark⠀that⠀doesn't⠀quite⠀fit,⠀a⠀silence⠀slightly⠀wrong⠀—⠀stated⠀at⠀the⠀same⠀pitch⠀as⠀the⠀coffee.\n\nAdvance⠀the⠀relationship⠀through⠀legible⠀small⠀changes:⠀a⠀disagreement⠀shown⠀by⠀an⠀object⠀set⠀down⠀too⠀carefully,⠀a⠀decision⠀about⠀staying⠀shown⠀by⠀the⠀narrator⠀finishing⠀a⠀task⠀that⠀could⠀have⠀been⠀left.⠀Let⠀aftermath⠀register⠀in⠀the⠀next⠀selected⠀detail⠀rather⠀than⠀a⠀summary.⠀The⠀narrator's⠀not-knowing⠀about⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀stays⠀unfilled⠀—⠀no⠀speculation⠀dressed⠀as⠀description.⠀Stop⠀when⠀the⠀chosen⠀details⠀have⠀done⠀their⠀work,⠀without⠀a⠀closing⠀explanation⠀or⠀emotional⠀tally.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajas::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Modern⠀Literature⠀/⠀Contemporary⠀Novel\n\nWrite⠀sustained⠀scene-first⠀prose.⠀Open⠀inside⠀a⠀particular⠀ongoing⠀moment⠀—⠀dinner⠀half-prepared,⠀a⠀drive⠀with⠀the⠀radio⠀low,⠀an⠀errand⠀running⠀long⠀—⠀and⠀let⠀the⠀scene⠀move⠀naturally⠀among⠀what⠀the⠀narrator⠀does,⠀what⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀says,⠀what⠀the⠀narrator⠀perceives,⠀remembers,⠀and⠀privately⠀feels.⠀Use⠀paragraphing⠀and⠀light⠀transitions⠀to⠀mark⠀shifts⠀of⠀attention⠀or⠀small⠀jumps⠀in⠀time;⠀no⠀recap⠀machinery,⠀no⠀stopping⠀to⠀explain⠀what⠀the⠀scene⠀means.⠀The⠀reader⠀assembles⠀the⠀relationship⠀from⠀accumulated⠀particular⠀moments,⠀not⠀from⠀stated⠀history.\n\nHold⠀the⠀surface⠀calm⠀and⠀exact.⠀Describe⠀tasks⠀at⠀their⠀real⠀pace⠀and⠀weight:⠀the⠀sound⠀of⠀the⠀door,⠀the⠀heft⠀of⠀the⠀bag,⠀the⠀table's⠀texture,⠀the⠀specific⠀way⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀performs⠀a⠀small⠀task.⠀Let⠀strangeness⠀or⠀trouble⠀enter⠀through⠀ordinary⠀means⠀—⠀a⠀remark⠀that⠀sits⠀wrong,⠀a⠀silence⠀longer⠀than⠀its⠀precedent,⠀a⠀familiar⠀room⠀feeling⠀slightly⠀other⠀—⠀described⠀evenly,⠀without⠀the⠀prose⠀signaling⠀alarm.⠀Interiority⠀belongs⠀to⠀the⠀narrator⠀and⠀is⠀rendered⠀directly⠀where⠀authorized:⠀private⠀worry,⠀memory,⠀the⠀arithmetic⠀of⠀staying⠀or⠀leaving.⠀Do⠀not⠀extend⠀that⠀access⠀to⠀the⠀other⠀person;⠀their⠀words,⠀faces,⠀and⠀actions⠀are⠀observed,⠀and⠀the⠀narrator's⠀readings⠀of⠀them⠀can⠀be⠀uncertain⠀or⠀mistaken.\n\nLet⠀the⠀relationship⠀develop⠀through⠀the⠀scene's⠀actual⠀events.⠀A⠀disclosure⠀can⠀land⠀mid-activity;⠀a⠀practical⠀disagreement⠀can⠀open⠀onto⠀a⠀larger⠀concern;⠀care⠀can⠀appear⠀as⠀one⠀person⠀remembering⠀a⠀detail⠀the⠀other⠀thought⠀forgotten.⠀Feel⠀the⠀aftermath⠀in⠀the⠀next⠀action⠀or⠀exchange⠀rather⠀than⠀announcing⠀a⠀turning⠀point.⠀The⠀scene⠀may⠀still⠀be⠀in⠀progress⠀when⠀it⠀ends⠀—⠀task⠀unfinished,⠀question⠀unanswered,⠀attention⠀still⠀on⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀—⠀and⠀the⠀novel's⠀flexible⠀attention⠀can⠀carry⠀whatever⠀comes⠀next.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajat::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Relationship-Centric⠀Fanfiction⠀(AO3-inspired)\n\nLet⠀the⠀supplied⠀premise⠀dictate⠀the⠀scenes.⠀If⠀the⠀premise⠀is⠀slow⠀development,⠀write⠀the⠀moment⠀one⠀person's⠀habits⠀have⠀become⠀familiar⠀to⠀the⠀other⠀—⠀the⠀particular⠀attention⠀that⠀no⠀longer⠀needs⠀explaining.⠀If⠀it⠀is⠀established⠀love,⠀write⠀the⠀private⠀language:⠀the⠀joke⠀only⠀they⠀make,⠀the⠀shorthand⠀for⠀an⠀old⠀disaster,⠀the⠀small⠀ritual⠀that⠀survives⠀bad⠀weeks.⠀If⠀it⠀is⠀repair,⠀write⠀the⠀specific⠀gesture⠀or⠀exchange⠀that⠀begins⠀restoring⠀trust,⠀and⠀let⠀trust⠀be⠀partial⠀and⠀slow⠀where⠀that⠀is⠀true⠀to⠀the⠀premise.⠀Use⠀only⠀the⠀premise⠀actually⠀supplied;⠀do⠀not⠀stock⠀the⠀scene⠀with⠀borrowed⠀tropes.\n\nBuild⠀depth⠀through⠀callbacks⠀that⠀change.⠀A⠀phrase⠀first⠀said⠀ironically,⠀later⠀said⠀in⠀earnest;⠀an⠀object⠀one⠀person⠀kept;⠀a⠀silence⠀that⠀recalls⠀an⠀earlier,⠀worse⠀silence⠀and⠀is⠀now⠀survivable.⠀Recurrence⠀should⠀measure⠀distance⠀traveled,⠀not⠀restate⠀the⠀earlier⠀beat.⠀Give⠀affection,⠀jealousy,⠀comfort,⠀rivalry,⠀or⠀discovery⠀the⠀space⠀it⠀needs⠀at⠀its⠀own⠀moment,⠀and⠀report⠀intimate⠀events⠀in⠀the⠀calm,⠀even⠀voice⠀the⠀narrator⠀uses:⠀emotional⠀weight⠀accumulates⠀from⠀specific⠀detail⠀rather⠀than⠀heightened⠀language,⠀and⠀an⠀intimate⠀moment⠀can⠀be⠀told⠀as⠀plainly⠀as⠀a⠀grocery⠀run.\n\nContain⠀the⠀material⠀in⠀unhurried⠀practical⠀activity⠀—⠀cooking⠀together,⠀waiting⠀for⠀a⠀call,⠀walking⠀a⠀known⠀route,⠀fixing⠀something⠀in⠀the⠀apartment⠀—⠀so⠀the⠀relationship⠀develops⠀through⠀attention⠀paid⠀during⠀ordinary⠀things.⠀Deliver⠀the⠀payoff⠀the⠀premise⠀promises⠀through⠀one⠀small,⠀exact⠀moment:⠀a⠀remembered⠀detail⠀produced⠀at⠀the⠀right⠀time,⠀a⠀hand⠀allowed⠀to⠀stay,⠀the⠀joke⠀finally⠀landing.⠀What⠀comes⠀after⠀may⠀stay⠀open;⠀the⠀scene⠀can⠀close⠀on⠀the⠀moment⠀itself,⠀with⠀the⠀future⠀of⠀the⠀two⠀of⠀them⠀still⠀theirs⠀to⠀decide.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajau::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Saga⠀/⠀Oral⠀Epic\n\nTell⠀the⠀relationship⠀as⠀an⠀account⠀of⠀the⠀deeds⠀by⠀which⠀these⠀two⠀people⠀will⠀remember⠀each⠀other.⠀A⠀repeated⠀kindness,⠀a⠀hard⠀conversation⠀held⠀anyway,⠀a⠀decision⠀made⠀in⠀an⠀unremarkable⠀place,⠀an⠀act⠀of⠀care⠀nobody⠀announced⠀—⠀each⠀can⠀enter⠀the⠀account⠀because⠀the⠀two⠀of⠀them⠀have⠀lived⠀with⠀its⠀consequences.⠀Work⠀with⠀concrete⠀particulars⠀as⠀the⠀chronicle's⠀material:⠀who⠀said⠀the⠀thing⠀first,⠀who⠀returned⠀to⠀it⠀later,⠀who⠀stayed⠀when⠀staying⠀was⠀inconvenient,⠀and⠀how⠀the⠀meaning⠀shifted⠀between⠀tellings.⠀Preserve⠀the⠀present⠀scene's⠀scale;⠀a⠀shared⠀meal⠀stays⠀a⠀shared⠀meal⠀even⠀when⠀it⠀belongs⠀to⠀a⠀longer⠀history⠀between⠀them.\n\nEstablish⠀people⠀and⠀acts⠀with⠀compact⠀declarations⠀—⠀the⠀one⠀who⠀came⠀back,⠀the⠀night⠀the⠀answer⠀changed⠀—⠀then⠀expand⠀into⠀the⠀particulars⠀that⠀make⠀the⠀declaration⠀incomplete.⠀Let⠀a⠀recurring⠀phrase⠀be⠀earned⠀by⠀an⠀established⠀moment⠀between⠀them⠀rather⠀than⠀a⠀decorative⠀tag⠀repeated⠀at⠀every⠀entrance,⠀and⠀return⠀to⠀it⠀when⠀a⠀later⠀occurrence⠀gives⠀it⠀a⠀new⠀application.⠀Keep⠀the⠀teller's⠀account⠀separate⠀from⠀the⠀other⠀person's⠀private⠀experience:⠀being⠀remembered⠀as⠀the⠀one⠀who⠀stayed⠀does⠀not⠀mean⠀staying⠀was⠀easy,⠀certain,⠀or⠀unregretted,⠀and⠀the⠀other⠀person's⠀reasons⠀remain⠀partly⠀their⠀own.\n\nLet⠀living⠀speech⠀interrupt⠀the⠀chronicle's⠀authority.⠀The⠀other⠀person,⠀present⠀in⠀the⠀scene,⠀may⠀object⠀to⠀a⠀detail,⠀correct⠀the⠀order⠀of⠀events,⠀or⠀answer⠀an⠀elevated⠀introduction⠀with⠀something⠀practical⠀—⠀the⠀kettle,⠀the⠀bill,⠀the⠀time.⠀This⠀need⠀not⠀become⠀parody;⠀humor⠀can⠀rise⠀from⠀the⠀persistence⠀of⠀a⠀private⠀story⠀without⠀turning⠀chores⠀into⠀battle⠀or⠀every⠀inconvenience⠀into⠀doom.⠀Keep⠀the⠀telling's⠀access⠀consistent⠀with⠀the⠀perspective⠀in⠀force.⠀The⠀account⠀can⠀end⠀with⠀the⠀relationship⠀still⠀being⠀made⠀—⠀another⠀modest⠀act⠀available⠀to⠀be⠀remembered,⠀and⠀what⠀will⠀be⠀said⠀about⠀these⠀two⠀left⠀open⠀rather⠀than⠀declared.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajav::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Scandinavian⠀Literary⠀Traditions\n\nWrite⠀the⠀romance⠀through⠀the⠀Scandinavian⠀domestic-realist⠀route:⠀a⠀composed⠀third-person⠀or⠀first-person⠀narrative⠀that⠀stays⠀close⠀to⠀the⠀practical⠀maintenance⠀of⠀a⠀shared⠀or⠀adjacent⠀life.⠀Let⠀the⠀relationship⠀become⠀legible⠀through⠀a⠀limited⠀set⠀of⠀repeated⠀domestic⠀anchors—one⠀meal,⠀one⠀route,⠀one⠀household⠀task,⠀one⠀object⠀that⠀changes⠀ownership⠀or⠀position.⠀Stay⠀with⠀those⠀anchors⠀across⠀scenes⠀so⠀that⠀their⠀shifting⠀condition⠀performs⠀the⠀emotional⠀development;⠀do⠀not⠀introduce⠀a⠀fresh⠀prop⠀for⠀every⠀feeling.\n\nTreat⠀each⠀anchor⠀as⠀part⠀of⠀Murakami's⠀exact-surface⠀method.⠀Render⠀it⠀with⠀unhurried⠀sensory⠀precision:⠀the⠀weight⠀of⠀a⠀shopping⠀bag,⠀the⠀click⠀of⠀a⠀lock,⠀the⠀temperature⠀of⠀a⠀stair⠀rail.⠀Then⠀let⠀a⠀later⠀change⠀in⠀that⠀same⠀surface⠀register⠀as⠀a⠀threshold⠀effect.⠀If⠀the⠀light⠀above⠀the⠀table⠀seems⠀different⠀one⠀evening,⠀keep⠀the⠀factual⠀scene⠀stable—the⠀bulb⠀has⠀not⠀changed,⠀the⠀weather⠀has⠀not⠀changed—and⠀let⠀the⠀disturbed⠀perception⠀belong⠀to⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀alone,⠀narrated⠀without⠀diagnosis⠀or⠀explanation.⠀The⠀other⠀person⠀remains⠀unaware⠀of⠀that⠀inward⠀shift⠀unless⠀it⠀surfaces⠀in⠀a⠀practical⠀change,⠀such⠀as⠀pausing⠀before⠀sitting⠀down⠀or⠀forgetting⠀to⠀offer⠀a⠀second⠀cup.\n\nThe⠀relationship⠀advances⠀through⠀small⠀material⠀acts⠀of⠀care⠀and⠀neglect,⠀but⠀do⠀not⠀treat⠀any⠀single⠀act⠀as⠀a⠀fixed⠀sign.⠀One⠀character⠀may⠀set⠀out⠀the⠀other's⠀cup⠀for⠀reasons⠀of⠀habit,⠀affection,⠀guilt,⠀or⠀distraction;⠀the⠀narrative⠀should⠀make⠀the⠀context⠀decide⠀its⠀meaning.⠀Pay⠀attention⠀to⠀the⠀order⠀and⠀timing⠀of⠀these⠀acts.⠀A⠀cup⠀set⠀out⠀before⠀the⠀other⠀arrives⠀differs⠀in⠀weight⠀from⠀a⠀cup⠀set⠀out⠀after⠀a⠀reproach.⠀When⠀a⠀gesture⠀is⠀repeated,⠀let⠀the⠀repetition⠀itself⠀be⠀the⠀evidence⠀of⠀a⠀changed⠀condition,⠀not⠀the⠀explanation⠀of⠀it.\n\nPrivate⠀feeling⠀appears⠀as⠀ordinary⠀nonspoken⠀interiority⠀tied⠀to⠀the⠀physical⠀task:⠀a⠀thought⠀while⠀peeling⠀potatoes,⠀a⠀memory⠀opened⠀by⠀a⠀particular⠀door⠀handle,⠀a⠀decision⠀formed⠀between⠀two⠀rooms.⠀Keep⠀it⠀strictly⠀within⠀the⠀viewpoint⠀character's⠀mind;⠀no⠀other⠀character⠀reads⠀it.⠀Disagreement⠀should⠀be⠀routed⠀through⠀the⠀practical⠀world⠀and⠀its⠀aftermath⠀felt⠀in⠀the⠀next⠀ordinary⠀action.⠀If⠀one⠀person⠀pays⠀a⠀bill⠀without⠀asking,⠀do⠀not⠀stage⠀the⠀response⠀as⠀a⠀confrontation⠀unless⠀the⠀actual⠀characters⠀would⠀speak;⠀let⠀the⠀other⠀leave⠀the⠀house⠀a⠀few⠀minutes⠀earlier⠀the⠀next⠀morning,⠀or⠀walk⠀the⠀longer⠀way⠀home.\n\nEnd⠀a⠀response⠀at⠀a⠀point⠀of⠀quiet⠀accumulation⠀rather⠀than⠀a⠀required⠀outcome.⠀You⠀may⠀close⠀after⠀a⠀completed⠀shared⠀task,⠀after⠀one⠀character⠀notices⠀a⠀familiar⠀object⠀has⠀been⠀moved,⠀or⠀after⠀a⠀private⠀thought⠀that⠀reshapes⠀the⠀day's⠀ordinary⠀calm.⠀A⠀declaration⠀or⠀reunion⠀is⠀permitted⠀only⠀if⠀the⠀actual⠀relationship⠀has⠀earned⠀it;⠀otherwise,⠀stop⠀with⠀the⠀next⠀meal,⠀the⠀next⠀errand,⠀or⠀the⠀next⠀silence.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajaw::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Screenplay\n\nWrite⠀the⠀romance⠀through⠀filmable⠀scenes⠀whose⠀progression⠀is⠀measured⠀by⠀returning⠀visible⠀and⠀audible⠀details.⠀Establish⠀two⠀or⠀three⠀concrete⠀anchors⠀in⠀the⠀early⠀scenes—a⠀particular⠀radio⠀station,⠀a⠀shopping⠀bag⠀hanging⠀on⠀the⠀same⠀hook,⠀the⠀sound⠀of⠀a⠀kettle⠀before⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀leaves.⠀Use⠀action⠀lines⠀to⠀record⠀these⠀details⠀with⠀Murakami's⠀exactness,⠀then⠀bring⠀them⠀back⠀in⠀later⠀scenes⠀with⠀different⠀conditions.⠀The⠀kettle⠀that⠀once⠀boiled⠀before⠀a⠀shared⠀breakfast⠀now⠀whistles⠀during⠀a⠀solitary⠀wait;⠀the⠀radio⠀can⠀be⠀left⠀on⠀in⠀an⠀empty⠀room.⠀The⠀changed⠀detail⠀carries⠀the⠀romantic⠀movement⠀without⠀explanatory⠀dialogue.\n\nLet⠀dialogue⠀stay⠀conversational⠀and⠀indirect,⠀but⠀structure⠀each⠀exchange⠀so⠀that⠀the⠀relationship⠀is⠀legible⠀through⠀what⠀is⠀not⠀said.⠀A⠀question⠀about⠀dinner⠀can⠀be⠀a⠀bid⠀for⠀the⠀other⠀person's⠀time;⠀a⠀remark⠀about⠀a⠀train⠀schedule⠀can⠀be⠀a⠀way⠀of⠀asking⠀whether⠀they⠀will⠀meet⠀again.⠀Write⠀the⠀pauses⠀as⠀action⠀lines,⠀not⠀as⠀stage⠀directions:⠀a⠀character⠀holds⠀a⠀cup,⠀folds⠀a⠀receipt,⠀or⠀looks⠀at⠀the⠀door⠀at⠀the⠀moment⠀when⠀a⠀more⠀direct⠀line⠀might⠀have⠀come.⠀This⠀keeps⠀the⠀subtext⠀visible⠀without⠀turning⠀every⠀silence⠀into⠀a⠀mandatory⠀emotional⠀beat.\n\nUse⠀offscreen⠀sound⠀only⠀when⠀it⠀carries⠀a⠀fact⠀the⠀audience⠀needs.⠀A⠀closing⠀door,⠀a⠀phone⠀vibrating,⠀or⠀rain⠀starting⠀can⠀announce⠀an⠀arrival⠀or⠀a⠀missed⠀connection.⠀Do⠀not⠀use⠀camera⠀commands.⠀Present⠀private⠀focal⠀experience⠀as⠀a⠀clearly⠀attributed⠀nonspoken⠀note⠀in⠀the⠀active⠀presentation,⠀distinct⠀from⠀dialogue⠀and⠀voice-over.⠀For⠀example,⠀after⠀an⠀action⠀line⠀shows⠀a⠀character⠀pausing⠀at⠀a⠀window,⠀a⠀note⠀may⠀record⠀that⠀they⠀are⠀remembering⠀the⠀last⠀time⠀they⠀stood⠀there.⠀No⠀other⠀character⠀can⠀hear⠀or⠀know⠀this⠀note.\n\nLet⠀timing⠀and⠀obligations⠀complicate⠀the⠀scenes⠀without⠀melodrama.⠀If⠀a⠀shift⠀at⠀work⠀forces⠀a⠀postponement,⠀show⠀the⠀practical⠀consequence⠀in⠀the⠀next⠀scene:⠀the⠀meal⠀is⠀cold,⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀has⠀already⠀left,⠀or⠀a⠀message⠀remains⠀unanswered.⠀The⠀scene⠀can⠀end⠀on⠀a⠀completed⠀action,⠀an⠀unfinished⠀sentence,⠀or⠀a⠀quiet⠀exit.⠀Do⠀not⠀force⠀a⠀confession,⠀a⠀kiss,⠀or⠀a⠀reunion;⠀the⠀changed⠀anchor⠀or⠀unresolved⠀pause⠀is⠀the⠀emotional⠀outcome.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajax::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Stage⠀Play\n\nBuild⠀the⠀romance⠀through⠀a⠀small⠀number⠀of⠀recurring⠀props⠀and⠀positions⠀that⠀the⠀characters⠀use⠀differently⠀over⠀the⠀play.⠀Choose⠀one⠀visible⠀object—a⠀coat⠀on⠀a⠀hook,⠀a⠀cup⠀left⠀near⠀a⠀chair,⠀a⠀radio⠀positioned⠀on⠀a⠀windowsill—and⠀return⠀to⠀it⠀in⠀at⠀least⠀two⠀scenes.⠀Stage⠀the⠀first⠀instance⠀with⠀neutral⠀physical⠀business:⠀a⠀character⠀hangs⠀the⠀coat⠀as⠀a⠀matter⠀of⠀routine.⠀Stage⠀the⠀later⠀instance⠀with⠀a⠀changed⠀action⠀or⠀absence:⠀the⠀coat⠀is⠀moved,⠀left⠀untouched,⠀or⠀hung⠀by⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀for⠀the⠀first⠀time.⠀The⠀audience⠀reads⠀the⠀relationship⠀through⠀that⠀difference⠀without⠀a⠀line⠀of⠀explanation.\n\nTreat⠀the⠀stage⠀space⠀itself⠀as⠀the⠀threshold⠀mechanism.⠀Let⠀the⠀ordinary⠀set⠀remain⠀factually⠀stable⠀while⠀one⠀character's⠀relation⠀to⠀it⠀shifts.⠀If⠀a⠀character⠀pauses⠀at⠀the⠀same⠀window⠀and⠀finds⠀the⠀light⠀altered,⠀do⠀not⠀change⠀the⠀lighting⠀cue⠀unless⠀the⠀world⠀changes;⠀instead,⠀write⠀the⠀pause⠀and⠀the⠀subsequent⠀behavior—a⠀step⠀back,⠀a⠀hand⠀raised⠀then⠀lowered—as⠀the⠀visible⠀sign⠀of⠀that⠀private⠀disturbance.⠀Another⠀character⠀may⠀ask⠀if⠀something⠀is⠀wrong,⠀but⠀the⠀reply⠀stays⠀indirect.⠀The⠀uncanny⠀is⠀carried⠀by⠀the⠀actor's⠀physical⠀relation⠀to⠀the⠀space,⠀not⠀by⠀supernatural⠀staging.\n\nWrite⠀dialogue⠀that⠀moves⠀around⠀the⠀central⠀feeling⠀through⠀practical⠀topics:⠀train⠀times,⠀a⠀broken⠀zipper,⠀a⠀song⠀half-remembered.⠀Structure⠀each⠀exchange⠀so⠀that⠀one⠀character's⠀attention⠀is⠀revealed⠀by⠀what⠀they⠀remember⠀or⠀offer.⠀A⠀line⠀about⠀picking⠀up⠀groceries⠀can⠀show⠀concern;⠀a⠀question⠀about⠀the⠀other⠀person's⠀coat⠀can⠀show⠀that⠀they⠀noticed⠀it⠀was⠀damp.⠀Do⠀not⠀let⠀every⠀pause⠀carry⠀a⠀labeled⠀emotion.⠀Instead,⠀pair⠀a⠀pause⠀with⠀a⠀small⠀stage⠀action—setting⠀down⠀a⠀bag,⠀touching⠀the⠀back⠀of⠀a⠀chair—that⠀lets⠀the⠀silence⠀mean⠀something⠀specific⠀in⠀the⠀moment.\n\nKeep⠀private⠀experience⠀as⠀nonspoken⠀authoring⠀material,⠀not⠀as⠀monologue⠀or⠀aside⠀unless⠀separately⠀authorized.⠀A⠀focal⠀note⠀may⠀record⠀that⠀a⠀character⠀notices⠀the⠀other⠀has⠀not⠀hung⠀up⠀their⠀coat⠀tonight,⠀or⠀that⠀they⠀are⠀waiting⠀for⠀a⠀question⠀that⠀does⠀not⠀come.⠀This⠀note⠀is⠀not⠀audible⠀to⠀anyone⠀on⠀stage.⠀Aftermath⠀should⠀be⠀staged⠀in⠀the⠀next⠀action⠀or⠀exit:⠀one⠀person⠀leaves⠀for⠀a⠀walk,⠀the⠀other⠀starts⠀washing⠀dishes⠀alone.⠀A⠀scene⠀may⠀end⠀on⠀a⠀line,⠀an⠀exit,⠀or⠀a⠀shared⠀task⠀completed⠀without⠀resolution.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajay::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Stream⠀of⠀Consciousness\n\nWrite⠀the⠀romance⠀through⠀a⠀single⠀authorized⠀mind⠀whose⠀movement⠀is⠀organized⠀by⠀two⠀or⠀three⠀recurring⠀anchor-images⠀from⠀ordinary⠀life.⠀Choose⠀a⠀concrete⠀present⠀object⠀or⠀sound—the⠀sound⠀of⠀a⠀kettle,⠀a⠀specific⠀bus⠀seat,⠀the⠀feel⠀of⠀a⠀coat⠀sleeve—and⠀use⠀it⠀as⠀the⠀point⠀of⠀return⠀whenever⠀a⠀memory⠀or⠀imagined⠀scene⠀begins⠀to⠀dissolve.⠀The⠀mind⠀may⠀travel⠀far⠀from⠀the⠀present⠀moment,⠀but⠀each⠀recollection⠀should⠀end⠀by⠀re-touching⠀the⠀anchor,⠀now⠀loaded⠀with⠀the⠀feeling⠀the⠀memory⠀added.⠀This⠀rhythmic⠀return⠀is⠀what⠀makes⠀the⠀stream⠀meaningful⠀rather⠀than⠀random.\n\nLet⠀Murakami's⠀exact⠀surfaces⠀open⠀the⠀memories.⠀Describe⠀the⠀present⠀anchor⠀with⠀precise⠀sensory⠀detail:⠀the⠀kettle's⠀whistle,⠀the⠀cold⠀metal⠀of⠀the⠀bus⠀pole,⠀the⠀weight⠀of⠀the⠀coat.⠀Then⠀allow⠀an⠀association⠀to⠀carry⠀the⠀mind⠀to⠀a⠀past⠀scene⠀with⠀the⠀same⠀or⠀a⠀related⠀surface—a⠀different⠀kettle,⠀an⠀earlier⠀bus⠀ride,⠀a⠀coat⠀left⠀behind.⠀The⠀memory⠀should⠀remain⠀tied⠀to⠀the⠀authorized⠀mind's⠀actual⠀experience,⠀not⠀a⠀generic⠀image.⠀Distinguish⠀clearly⠀between⠀present⠀perception⠀and⠀remembered⠀scene:⠀use⠀present⠀tense⠀for⠀the⠀current⠀moment⠀and⠀past⠀or⠀conditional⠀for⠀memory⠀and⠀imagination.⠀If⠀the⠀mind⠀drifts⠀into⠀an⠀imagined⠀conversation,⠀mark⠀it⠀as⠀such,⠀and⠀return⠀to⠀the⠀anchor⠀before⠀another⠀association⠀begins.\n\nDevelop⠀the⠀relationship⠀through⠀the⠀accumulation⠀of⠀remembered⠀details,⠀not⠀through⠀chronological⠀report.⠀The⠀mind⠀may⠀notice⠀that⠀it⠀has⠀started⠀checking⠀for⠀the⠀other⠀person's⠀shoes⠀by⠀the⠀door,⠀or⠀that⠀a⠀phrase⠀once⠀neutral⠀now⠀causes⠀a⠀bodily⠀response.⠀Let⠀these⠀observations⠀surface⠀during⠀the⠀stream⠀rather⠀than⠀being⠀stated⠀as⠀conclusions.⠀When⠀the⠀same⠀memory⠀returns⠀later,⠀let⠀it⠀appear⠀changed—shorter,⠀sharper,⠀or⠀accompanied⠀by⠀a⠀new⠀association—so⠀that⠀the⠀reader⠀feels⠀the⠀mind's⠀emotional⠀development⠀through⠀the⠀revision⠀of⠀its⠀own⠀recurring⠀material.\n\nAllow⠀interruptions⠀to⠀enter⠀and⠀redirect⠀the⠀thought,⠀but⠀always⠀bring⠀the⠀stream⠀back⠀to⠀the⠀anchor⠀before⠀the⠀interruption⠀ends.⠀If⠀a⠀timer⠀goes⠀off,⠀use⠀it⠀as⠀the⠀new⠀present⠀surface,⠀then⠀allow⠀the⠀next⠀memory⠀to⠀open⠀from⠀that⠀sound.⠀The⠀response⠀can⠀stop⠀at⠀the⠀anchor,⠀at⠀a⠀new⠀perception,⠀or⠀at⠀a⠀bodily⠀sensation⠀that⠀interrupts⠀a⠀long⠀memory.⠀No⠀decision,⠀confession,⠀or⠀completed⠀encounter⠀is⠀required;⠀the⠀final⠀moment⠀is⠀the⠀mind's⠀alighting⠀on⠀a⠀surface⠀after⠀its⠀circling.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajaz::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Text⠀Messages⠀/⠀Chat⠀Transcript\n\nWrite⠀the⠀romance⠀through⠀a⠀transcript⠀governed⠀by⠀a⠀small⠀set⠀of⠀recurring⠀digital⠀details—one⠀timestamp,⠀one⠀draft⠀behavior,⠀one⠀read-receipt⠀pattern—that⠀gain⠀meaning⠀through⠀repetition.⠀Choose⠀a⠀particular⠀sender's⠀habit,⠀such⠀as⠀always⠀erasing⠀the⠀first⠀word,⠀answering⠀after⠀exactly⠀one⠀minute⠀when⠀anxious,⠀or⠀leaving⠀the⠀read⠀receipt⠀on⠀without⠀replying.⠀Return⠀to⠀that⠀habit⠀at⠀least⠀twice,⠀so⠀its⠀later⠀appearance⠀or⠀absence⠀carries⠀the⠀relationship's⠀change.⠀The⠀exact⠀detail⠀becomes⠀the⠀Murakami⠀surface.\n\nLet⠀the⠀messages⠀themselves⠀remain⠀unhurried⠀and⠀slightly⠀indirect.⠀Write⠀them⠀as⠀conversational⠀fragments⠀about⠀groceries,⠀trains,⠀a⠀song⠀heard⠀in⠀a⠀shop.⠀Do⠀not⠀make⠀every⠀message⠀emotionally⠀portentous.⠀The⠀romantic⠀movement⠀should⠀be⠀legible⠀in⠀the⠀difference⠀between⠀messages⠀over⠀time:⠀the⠀same⠀question⠀asked⠀in⠀a⠀different⠀way,⠀the⠀first⠀repeated⠀phrase,⠀the⠀first⠀mention⠀of⠀the⠀other's⠀daily⠀routine.⠀Structure⠀the⠀exchange⠀so⠀that⠀a⠀later⠀message⠀refers⠀to⠀an⠀earlier⠀one—a⠀callback⠀not⠀as⠀a⠀joke⠀but⠀as⠀proof⠀of⠀attention.\n\nUse⠀interface⠀events⠀as⠀punctuation,⠀not⠀as⠀explanation.⠀A⠀long⠀delay⠀after⠀a⠀question,⠀an⠀edit⠀that⠀changes⠀a⠀word,⠀or⠀a⠀draft⠀left⠀unsent⠀should⠀be⠀documented⠀with⠀the⠀style's⠀permitted⠀notational⠀forms.⠀But⠀do⠀not⠀attach⠀a⠀fixed⠀emotion⠀to⠀the⠀event.⠀Let⠀the⠀reader⠀infer⠀from⠀the⠀surrounding⠀messages⠀and⠀from⠀what⠀the⠀sender⠀does⠀next.⠀If⠀a⠀character⠀sends⠀a⠀message⠀then⠀edits⠀it⠀to⠀remove⠀a⠀direct⠀question,⠀the⠀edit⠀is⠀evidence⠀of⠀hesitation,⠀not⠀proof⠀of⠀secrecy.⠀The⠀other⠀character⠀may⠀notice⠀or⠀not,⠀and⠀their⠀response⠀will⠀further⠀shape⠀the⠀meaning.\n\nPrivate⠀thought⠀must⠀be⠀clearly⠀separated⠀from⠀transmitted⠀text.⠀When⠀a⠀focal⠀character's⠀interiority⠀is⠀required,⠀present⠀it⠀as⠀a⠀nonspoken⠀context⠀outside⠀the⠀timestamped⠀exchange,⠀attributed⠀to⠀that⠀character⠀and⠀unavailable⠀to⠀the⠀other.⠀Do⠀not⠀use⠀unsent⠀drafts⠀as⠀a⠀metaphor⠀for⠀private⠀thought;⠀an⠀unsent⠀draft⠀is⠀evidence⠀of⠀an⠀interrupted⠀or⠀abandoned⠀act,⠀not⠀a⠀transparent⠀window⠀into⠀the⠀mind.⠀The⠀response⠀can⠀end⠀after⠀a⠀sent⠀message,⠀a⠀draft⠀left⠀unfinished,⠀a⠀delay,⠀or⠀a⠀quiet⠀interval.⠀No⠀confession⠀or⠀reunion⠀is⠀required;⠀the⠀next⠀message⠀is⠀the⠀continuation.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajba::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Visual⠀Novel\n\nWrite⠀the⠀romance⠀as⠀scene-oriented⠀passages⠀with⠀concise⠀Murakami-style⠀settings⠀and⠀alternating⠀dialogue⠀and⠀focal⠀narration.⠀Choose⠀a⠀recurring⠀background⠀element—a⠀window,⠀a⠀kitchen⠀counter,⠀a⠀station⠀platform—and⠀repeat⠀it⠀across⠀at⠀least⠀two⠀scenes.⠀Describe⠀it⠀with⠀precise⠀visual⠀wording⠀the⠀first⠀time,⠀then⠀let⠀its⠀reappearance⠀carry⠀the⠀romantic⠀change.⠀The⠀same⠀window⠀is⠀ordinary⠀in⠀one⠀scene⠀and⠀significant⠀in⠀another⠀because⠀of⠀what⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀now⠀associates⠀with⠀it⠀or⠀how⠀the⠀light⠀falls⠀during⠀a⠀shared⠀wait.\n\nLet⠀each⠀scene's⠀rhythm⠀be:⠀a⠀brief⠀exact⠀description,⠀then⠀dialogue,⠀then⠀a⠀focal⠀reaction⠀that⠀may⠀be⠀unspoken.⠀Keep⠀the⠀dialogue⠀conversational⠀and⠀slightly⠀indirect.⠀A⠀question⠀about⠀tea⠀can⠀be⠀a⠀bid⠀for⠀the⠀other⠀person's⠀time;⠀a⠀remark⠀about⠀a⠀song⠀can⠀be⠀a⠀reference⠀to⠀an⠀earlier⠀scene.⠀Use⠀background⠀cues⠀as⠀anchors,⠀not⠀as⠀truth⠀indicators.⠀If⠀a⠀character⠀looks⠀away,⠀that⠀expression⠀may⠀earn⠀attention,⠀but⠀the⠀relationship's⠀evidence⠀comes⠀from⠀what⠀they⠀do⠀or⠀say⠀next.⠀Do⠀not⠀add⠀branching⠀menus,⠀player⠀decisions,⠀or⠀romance⠀routes.\n\nPrivate⠀focal⠀experience⠀should⠀appear⠀as⠀ordinary⠀nonspoken⠀narration⠀tied⠀to⠀the⠀scene's⠀action⠀or⠀object.⠀A⠀thought⠀while⠀looking⠀at⠀a⠀closed⠀door,⠀a⠀memory⠀triggered⠀by⠀a⠀song,⠀a⠀decision⠀to⠀say⠀nothing⠀yet.⠀The⠀other⠀character⠀does⠀not⠀know⠀this⠀interiority.⠀Place⠀the⠀thought⠀after⠀a⠀visible⠀cue,⠀so⠀that⠀the⠀illustrated⠀scene⠀can⠀show⠀the⠀pause⠀and⠀the⠀text⠀can⠀reveal⠀the⠀mind's⠀movement.⠀Keep⠀the⠀thoughts⠀brief⠀and⠀focused⠀on⠀the⠀present⠀romantic⠀concern.\n\nLet⠀timing⠀and⠀obligation⠀shape⠀the⠀scenes⠀without⠀melodrama.⠀If⠀one⠀character⠀must⠀leave,⠀show⠀the⠀practical⠀detail—a⠀coat⠀taken,⠀a⠀bag⠀left⠀on⠀the⠀counter—and⠀then⠀let⠀the⠀focal⠀reaction⠀register⠀the⠀aftereffect.⠀A⠀scene⠀may⠀end⠀on⠀a⠀quiet⠀exchange,⠀a⠀postponed⠀question,⠀or⠀a⠀character⠀alone⠀with⠀a⠀newly⠀noticed⠀detail.⠀The⠀next⠀scene⠀can⠀open⠀with⠀a⠀different⠀location⠀but⠀should⠀carry⠀forward⠀one⠀of⠀the⠀recurring⠀elements,⠀so⠀that⠀the⠀visual⠀novel's⠀structure⠀accumulates⠀relationship⠀evidence.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamajbb::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Web⠀Serial\n\nWrite⠀the⠀romance⠀as⠀installment-oriented⠀prose⠀where⠀each⠀reply⠀contains⠀at⠀least⠀one⠀callback⠀to⠀a⠀previously⠀established⠀concrete⠀detail.⠀Maintain⠀a⠀short⠀inventory⠀of⠀recurring⠀objects,⠀phrases,⠀or⠀places—an⠀umbrella,⠀a⠀particular⠀song,⠀the⠀way⠀one⠀person⠀says⠀'later'—and⠀bring⠀one⠀of⠀them⠀back⠀whenever⠀the⠀relationship⠀changes⠀or⠀the⠀reader⠀needs⠀reorientation.⠀Describe⠀the⠀callback⠀in⠀its⠀new⠀condition,⠀not⠀as⠀a⠀summary.⠀If⠀the⠀umbrella⠀was⠀left⠀behind⠀in⠀an⠀early⠀chapter,⠀a⠀later⠀chapter⠀may⠀show⠀it⠀now⠀folded⠀by⠀the⠀door,⠀or⠀still⠀missing.⠀The⠀changed⠀object⠀carries⠀the⠀emotional⠀development.\n\nUse⠀Murakami's⠀unhurried⠀exactness⠀for⠀each⠀detail.⠀Name⠀the⠀object,⠀the⠀time,⠀the⠀sound,⠀or⠀the⠀small⠀action.⠀The⠀detail⠀should⠀be⠀concrete⠀enough⠀to⠀be⠀remembered⠀across⠀installments.⠀Let⠀the⠀relationship⠀accumulate⠀through⠀shifts⠀in⠀these⠀details:⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀starts⠀leaving⠀earlier,⠀a⠀question⠀keeps⠀being⠀postponed,⠀a⠀familiar⠀phrase⠀now⠀appears⠀in⠀a⠀different⠀context.⠀Do⠀not⠀force⠀a⠀cliffhanger.⠀Instead,⠀end⠀an⠀installment⠀at⠀a⠀point⠀where⠀the⠀callback⠀has⠀just⠀occurred⠀or⠀is⠀about⠀to⠀occur,⠀so⠀that⠀the⠀reader⠀carries⠀the⠀detail⠀into⠀the⠀next⠀reply.\n\nLet⠀timing⠀and⠀competing⠀wants⠀create⠀complications⠀with⠀meaningful⠀aftermath.⠀If⠀a⠀work⠀shift⠀or⠀family⠀obligation⠀changes⠀the⠀available⠀moment,⠀show⠀the⠀practical⠀consequence⠀in⠀the⠀same⠀or⠀next⠀installment:⠀a⠀silence⠀at⠀dinner,⠀a⠀route⠀changed,⠀a⠀message⠀left⠀unanswered.⠀Keep⠀required⠀private⠀experience⠀as⠀ordinary⠀nonspoken⠀interiority⠀when⠀it⠀contributes⠀to⠀the⠀feeling⠀or⠀thought,⠀even⠀if⠀no⠀immediate⠀decision⠀changes.⠀The⠀focal⠀character's⠀thought⠀can⠀revisit⠀an⠀earlier⠀detail⠀and⠀find⠀it⠀altered.\n\nA⠀response⠀may⠀close⠀on⠀completed⠀work,⠀a⠀pending⠀question,⠀a⠀quiet⠀realization,⠀or⠀a⠀character⠀alone⠀with⠀a⠀familiar⠀object.⠀Do⠀not⠀require⠀a⠀confession,⠀reunion,⠀or⠀reversal⠀at⠀every⠀boundary.⠀Instead,⠀let⠀the⠀installment's⠀end⠀function⠀as⠀a⠀pause⠀in⠀the⠀reader's⠀attention,⠀with⠀the⠀next⠀installment⠀opening⠀by⠀returning⠀to⠀the⠀same⠀detail⠀in⠀a⠀new⠀light.⠀Serial⠀duration⠀should⠀give⠀selected⠀emotional⠀details⠀room⠀to⠀acquire⠀meaning,⠀not⠀make⠀the⠀relationship⠀perpetually⠀recede.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamakaa::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Angsty⠀/⠀Emotionally⠀Turbulent\n\nTreat⠀every⠀courteous⠀exchange⠀as⠀a⠀possible⠀site⠀of⠀injury.⠀A⠀character⠀may⠀perform⠀the⠀correct⠀reply⠀while⠀privately⠀registering⠀what⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀has⠀just⠀admitted,⠀avoided,⠀or⠀assumed.⠀Use⠀the⠀Austen⠀profile's⠀social⠀reading⠀to⠀make⠀the⠀gap⠀between⠀public⠀composure⠀and⠀private⠀feeling⠀the⠀central⠀source⠀of⠀strain:⠀a⠀considerate⠀question⠀can⠀expose⠀an⠀old⠀grievance,⠀and⠀a⠀polite⠀refusal⠀can⠀be⠀more⠀wounding⠀than⠀an⠀open⠀quarrel.\n\nLet⠀the⠀viewpoint⠀character⠀interpret⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀through⠀the⠀available⠀social⠀evidence—tone,⠀timing,⠀omission,⠀the⠀choice⠀to⠀speak⠀or⠀not⠀speak—without⠀making⠀that⠀interpretation⠀reliable.⠀The⠀narration⠀may⠀follow⠀a⠀character's⠀free⠀indirect⠀reasoning⠀as⠀they⠀turn⠀a⠀small⠀remark⠀into⠀proof⠀of⠀indifference⠀or⠀lingering⠀affection,⠀then⠀show⠀the⠀next⠀exchange⠀complicating⠀that⠀conclusion.⠀Keep⠀the⠀reasoning⠀owned⠀by⠀the⠀character:⠀their⠀inference⠀is⠀not⠀the⠀narrator's⠀verdict,⠀and⠀the⠀other⠀person's⠀actual⠀motive⠀may⠀remain⠀partly⠀inaccessible.\n\nMake⠀emotional⠀cost⠀concrete⠀in⠀what⠀follows⠀the⠀difficult⠀moment.⠀After⠀a⠀confession,⠀apology,⠀or⠀withdrawal,⠀show⠀the⠀characters⠀continuing⠀their⠀practical⠀lives⠀with⠀altered⠀attention:⠀a⠀task⠀becomes⠀harder⠀to⠀finish,⠀a⠀room⠀feels⠀less⠀habitable,⠀a⠀planned⠀courtesy⠀is⠀performed⠀with⠀visible⠀effort.⠀Do⠀not⠀require⠀the⠀relationship⠀to⠀collapse⠀or⠀heal.⠀Warmth⠀may⠀appear⠀as⠀an⠀awkward,⠀partial⠀gesture⠀that⠀does⠀not⠀cancel⠀the⠀pain,⠀and⠀comfort⠀may⠀arrive⠀without⠀resolving⠀the⠀underlying⠀need.\n\nUse⠀the⠀romance⠀genre's⠀focus⠀on⠀belonging⠀together⠀to⠀keep⠀the⠀stakes⠀relational⠀rather⠀than⠀merely⠀atmospheric.⠀The⠀characters'⠀decisions⠀about⠀whether⠀to⠀stay,⠀return,⠀explain,⠀or⠀remain⠀silent⠀should⠀carry⠀consequences⠀for⠀their⠀sense⠀of⠀themselves⠀and⠀each⠀other.⠀Allow⠀competing⠀obligations⠀and⠀uncertainty⠀to⠀delay⠀or⠀complicate⠀those⠀decisions,⠀but⠀do⠀not⠀make⠀either⠀character⠀a⠀guaranteed⠀reward⠀or⠀a⠀fixed⠀source⠀of⠀suffering.⠀The⠀ending⠀may⠀leave⠀the⠀relationship⠀unsettled,⠀with⠀the⠀emotional⠀work⠀still⠀in⠀progress.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamakab::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Chat⠀Roleplay\n\nWrite⠀the⠀scene⠀in⠀readable⠀paragraphs⠀with⠀unmistakable⠀dialogue⠀attribution,⠀keeping⠀each⠀speaker's⠀words⠀and⠀actions⠀clearly⠀separated.⠀Use⠀the⠀Austen⠀profile's⠀social⠀attention⠀to⠀make⠀small⠀exchanges⠀carry⠀relational⠀meaning:⠀an⠀offer,⠀a⠀hesitation,⠀a⠀remembered⠀obligation,⠀or⠀a⠀courteous⠀phrase⠀can⠀reveal⠀what⠀a⠀character⠀wants⠀without⠀requiring⠀them⠀to⠀announce⠀it.⠀Let⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀notice⠀these⠀signals⠀and⠀interpret⠀them⠀through⠀their⠀own⠀assumptions,⠀while⠀the⠀other⠀characters'⠀private⠀motives⠀remain⠀available⠀only⠀through⠀what⠀they⠀say⠀and⠀do.\n\nGive⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀owned⠀interiority⠀that⠀accompanies⠀the⠀visible⠀scene.⠀Their⠀private⠀reasoning⠀may⠀run⠀alongside⠀the⠀conversation,⠀responding⠀to⠀a⠀remark⠀with⠀suspicion,⠀hope,⠀embarrassment,⠀or⠀a⠀revised⠀understanding⠀of⠀the⠀other⠀person.⠀Do⠀not⠀grant⠀access⠀to⠀minds⠀the⠀active⠀authorship⠀contract⠀excludes.⠀The⠀focal⠀character's⠀reading⠀of⠀another⠀person⠀is⠀an⠀inference,⠀not⠀a⠀confirmed⠀fact,⠀and⠀the⠀next⠀line⠀of⠀dialogue⠀may⠀support⠀or⠀complicate⠀it.\n\nAdvance⠀the⠀relationship⠀through⠀the⠀actual⠀interaction⠀rather⠀than⠀through⠀summary.⠀Let⠀attention,⠀memory,⠀proximity,⠀disclosure,⠀disagreement,⠀and⠀care⠀appear⠀in⠀concrete⠀moments:⠀a⠀character⠀recalls⠀an⠀earlier⠀conversation,⠀chooses⠀to⠀sit⠀nearer,⠀answers⠀a⠀question⠀with⠀more⠀honesty⠀than⠀intended,⠀or⠀performs⠀a⠀small⠀service⠀that⠀changes⠀the⠀emotional⠀register.⠀Keep⠀the⠀world⠀and⠀other⠀characters⠀active,⠀with⠀their⠀own⠀practical⠀concerns⠀continuing⠀around⠀the⠀central⠀exchange.\n\nEnd⠀the⠀response⠀at⠀a⠀natural⠀continuation⠀point⠀that⠀follows⠀from⠀the⠀scene.⠀The⠀next⠀speaker⠀may⠀respond⠀to⠀what⠀was⠀just⠀said,⠀a⠀task⠀may⠀remain⠀unfinished,⠀or⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀may⠀be⠀left⠀with⠀a⠀new⠀uncertainty.⠀Do⠀not⠀force⠀a⠀question,⠀cliffhanger,⠀or⠀choice⠀screen⠀at⠀the⠀end.⠀The⠀scene⠀may⠀pause⠀during⠀continuing⠀speech,⠀action,⠀thought,⠀or⠀an⠀unfinished⠀setup,⠀and⠀the⠀relationship⠀need⠀not⠀reach⠀a⠀resolution⠀before⠀the⠀reply⠀stops.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamakac::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Chinese⠀Literary⠀Traditions\n\nUse⠀the⠀intimate⠀urban⠀or⠀domestic⠀narrative⠀route⠀from⠀the⠀Chinese⠀literary⠀traditions⠀profile.⠀Keep⠀the⠀telling⠀close⠀to⠀a⠀particular⠀household,⠀courtyard,⠀apartment,⠀shop,⠀or⠀neighborhood,⠀and⠀let⠀the⠀relationship⠀develop⠀through⠀the⠀small⠀exchanges⠀that⠀occur⠀in⠀those⠀spaces:⠀a⠀shared⠀meal,⠀a⠀family⠀obligation,⠀a⠀neighbor's⠀comment,⠀a⠀gift⠀offered⠀or⠀refused,⠀a⠀conversation⠀interrupted⠀by⠀practical⠀duties.⠀The⠀setting's⠀language,⠀period,⠀and⠀community⠀should⠀remain⠀distinct⠀and⠀supplied⠀by⠀the⠀actual⠀story⠀rather⠀than⠀imported⠀as⠀decoration.\n\nApply⠀the⠀Austen⠀profile's⠀social⠀interpretation⠀to⠀the⠀community's⠀own⠀forms⠀of⠀courtesy,⠀obligation,⠀money,⠀and⠀reputation.⠀A⠀character's⠀standing⠀may⠀depend⠀on⠀family⠀connections,⠀work,⠀education,⠀housing,⠀or⠀the⠀judgments⠀of⠀elders⠀and⠀neighbors.⠀Let⠀these⠀pressures⠀give⠀a⠀small⠀exchange⠀several⠀meanings:⠀an⠀apparently⠀ordinary⠀visit⠀may⠀be⠀understood⠀as⠀an⠀inquiry⠀into⠀a⠀family's⠀circumstances,⠀and⠀a⠀polite⠀phrase⠀may⠀carry⠀an⠀unspoken⠀request⠀or⠀refusal.⠀Keep⠀the⠀viewpoint⠀character's⠀free⠀indirect⠀reasoning⠀owned⠀by⠀that⠀character,⠀so⠀their⠀reading⠀of⠀another⠀person's⠀behavior⠀is⠀an⠀inference⠀rather⠀than⠀a⠀confirmed⠀truth.\n\nOrganize⠀the⠀romance⠀around⠀attention,⠀memory,⠀proximity,⠀disclosure,⠀disagreement,⠀and⠀care.⠀The⠀characters⠀may⠀notice⠀each⠀other's⠀habits,⠀remember⠀an⠀earlier⠀meeting⠀differently,⠀find⠀themselves⠀repeatedly⠀placed⠀together⠀by⠀family⠀or⠀work,⠀reveal⠀something⠀they⠀had⠀intended⠀to⠀conceal,⠀or⠀disagree⠀about⠀a⠀practical⠀decision⠀that⠀exposes⠀their⠀different⠀positions.⠀Let⠀timing⠀and⠀competing⠀obligations⠀complicate⠀their⠀decisions⠀about⠀belonging⠀together.⠀The⠀relationship's⠀aftermath⠀should⠀be⠀meaningful,⠀but⠀neither⠀character⠀is⠀a⠀guaranteed⠀reward,⠀and⠀the⠀community's⠀expectations⠀need⠀not⠀determine⠀the⠀outcome.\n\nKeep⠀the⠀narrative⠀movement⠀composed⠀and⠀continuous,⠀with⠀the⠀intimate⠀route's⠀attention⠀to⠀domestic⠀detail⠀serving⠀the⠀relationship⠀rather⠀than⠀replacing⠀it.⠀Do⠀not⠀switch⠀into⠀martial⠀adventure,⠀experimental⠀construction,⠀or⠀broad⠀social⠀satire⠀unless⠀the⠀active⠀scene⠀already⠀requires⠀that⠀register.⠀The⠀Austen⠀irony⠀remains⠀available,⠀but⠀it⠀should⠀arise⠀from⠀the⠀contrast⠀between⠀what⠀a⠀character⠀believes⠀and⠀what⠀the⠀scene⠀reveals,⠀not⠀from⠀a⠀narrator's⠀detached⠀commentary⠀on⠀the⠀whole⠀community.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamakad::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Compressed⠀Gritty⠀Prose\n\nWrite⠀with⠀forceful⠀diction⠀and⠀compressed⠀transitions.⠀Move⠀from⠀one⠀concrete⠀moment⠀to⠀the⠀next⠀without⠀extended⠀social⠀framing,⠀letting⠀the⠀physical⠀scene⠀carry⠀the⠀relationship's⠀stakes:⠀a⠀worn⠀collar,⠀a⠀cracked⠀basin,⠀a⠀door⠀held⠀open⠀too⠀long,⠀a⠀coin⠀counted⠀twice,⠀a⠀chair⠀pulled⠀closer⠀or⠀left⠀where⠀it⠀stood.⠀Use⠀material⠀wear⠀and⠀practical⠀detail⠀to⠀show⠀what⠀the⠀characters⠀can⠀afford,⠀what⠀they⠀must⠀manage,⠀and⠀what⠀they⠀notice⠀about⠀each⠀other's⠀circumstances.\n\nApply⠀the⠀Austen⠀profile's⠀social⠀interpretation⠀through⠀observation⠀rather⠀than⠀elaboration.⠀A⠀character⠀may⠀read⠀another⠀person's⠀situation⠀from⠀a⠀single⠀telling⠀detail—the⠀state⠀of⠀their⠀shoes,⠀the⠀way⠀they⠀handle⠀money,⠀the⠀pause⠀before⠀they⠀accept⠀an⠀offer—and⠀that⠀reading⠀should⠀carry⠀the⠀weight⠀of⠀courtesy,⠀obligation,⠀family,⠀or⠀reputation.⠀Keep⠀the⠀viewpoint⠀character's⠀free⠀indirect⠀judgment⠀owned⠀by⠀them:⠀their⠀inference⠀is⠀sharp⠀and⠀particular,⠀not⠀a⠀narrator's⠀general⠀pronouncement.⠀Let⠀the⠀next⠀concrete⠀event⠀support⠀or⠀complicate⠀it.\n\nLet⠀the⠀romance⠀develop⠀through⠀attention,⠀memory,⠀proximity,⠀disclosure,⠀disagreement,⠀and⠀care⠀rendered⠀in⠀hard-edged⠀terms.⠀Attention⠀may⠀mean⠀noticing⠀a⠀habit⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀tries⠀to⠀hide.⠀Memory⠀may⠀return⠀as⠀an⠀unwanted⠀image⠀at⠀a⠀practical⠀moment.⠀Proximity⠀may⠀be⠀physical⠀and⠀charged,⠀with⠀the⠀characters⠀aware⠀of⠀the⠀space⠀between⠀them.⠀Disclosure⠀may⠀be⠀blunt,⠀partial,⠀or⠀forced⠀by⠀circumstance.⠀Disagreement⠀may⠀turn⠀practical,⠀with⠀the⠀argument⠀conducted⠀through⠀objects⠀and⠀tasks⠀as⠀much⠀as⠀words.⠀Care⠀may⠀appear⠀as⠀a⠀rough,⠀efficient⠀act⠀that⠀costs⠀the⠀giver⠀something.\n\nKeep⠀the⠀prose⠀varied⠀in⠀rhythm.⠀Use⠀short,⠀direct⠀sentences⠀for⠀impact,⠀but⠀retain⠀a⠀longer⠀thought⠀when⠀the⠀character's⠀reasoning⠀needs⠀room⠀to⠀move⠀through⠀a⠀difficult⠀inference⠀or⠀a⠀remembered⠀exchange.⠀Ground⠀abrasive⠀or⠀rough⠀speech⠀in⠀its⠀speaker's⠀actual⠀situation⠀and⠀temperament;⠀do⠀not⠀make⠀every⠀character⠀hard-edged⠀in⠀the⠀same⠀way.⠀The⠀emotional⠀stakes⠀remain⠀romantic—belonging,⠀trust,⠀vulnerability,⠀chosen⠀connection—but⠀they⠀are⠀rendered⠀through⠀pressure,⠀material⠀consequence,⠀and⠀the⠀effort⠀of⠀continuing.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamakae::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Epistolary⠀/⠀Documents\n\nTell⠀the⠀relationship⠀through⠀documents,⠀each⠀with⠀a⠀clear⠀author,⠀intended⠀recipient⠀or⠀purpose,⠀and⠀time⠀of⠀composition.⠀Use⠀the⠀specific⠀form⠀the⠀scene⠀requires—a⠀letter,⠀a⠀journal⠀entry,⠀a⠀note,⠀a⠀household⠀record,⠀an⠀invitation,⠀a⠀reply—rather⠀than⠀rotating⠀through⠀formats.⠀What⠀each⠀document⠀knows⠀or⠀conceals⠀follows⠀from⠀its⠀author's⠀situation:⠀a⠀letter⠀to⠀a⠀parent⠀may⠀omit⠀what⠀a⠀journal⠀entry⠀admits,⠀and⠀a⠀note⠀to⠀the⠀beloved⠀may⠀be⠀more⠀guarded⠀than⠀a⠀letter⠀to⠀a⠀trusted⠀friend.\n\nApply⠀the⠀Austen⠀profile's⠀social⠀interpretation⠀to⠀the⠀document's⠀rhetoric.⠀Courtesy,⠀offers,⠀omissions,⠀money,⠀family,⠀and⠀reputation⠀should⠀give⠀a⠀written⠀phrase⠀several⠀meanings.⠀A⠀writer⠀may⠀use⠀politeness⠀to⠀keep⠀distance,⠀mention⠀a⠀practical⠀matter⠀to⠀avoid⠀a⠀feeling,⠀or⠀offer⠀help⠀as⠀a⠀way⠀of⠀asking⠀to⠀be⠀needed.⠀Let⠀the⠀reader⠀infer⠀what⠀the⠀writer⠀believes⠀about⠀themselves⠀from⠀their⠀selection⠀and⠀emphasis,⠀while⠀keeping⠀the⠀document's⠀actual⠀words⠀as⠀the⠀only⠀access⠀to⠀that⠀writer's⠀mind.⠀Do⠀not⠀add⠀an⠀omniscient⠀explanation⠀after⠀every⠀record;⠀let⠀the⠀gaps⠀and⠀contradictions⠀work.\n\nAdvance⠀the⠀romance⠀through⠀the⠀sequence⠀of⠀documents.⠀Attention⠀may⠀appear⠀as⠀a⠀remembered⠀detail⠀in⠀a⠀letter.⠀Memory⠀may⠀be⠀revised⠀in⠀a⠀later⠀journal⠀entry.⠀Proximity⠀may⠀be⠀reported,⠀requested,⠀or⠀avoided⠀through⠀an⠀invitation⠀and⠀its⠀refusal.⠀Disclosure⠀may⠀be⠀partial,⠀delayed,⠀or⠀retracted⠀in⠀a⠀subsequent⠀note.⠀Disagreement⠀may⠀be⠀conducted⠀across⠀letters,⠀with⠀each⠀writer⠀interpreting⠀the⠀other's⠀silence⠀or⠀phrasing.⠀Care⠀may⠀be⠀shown⠀in⠀practical⠀arrangements⠀recorded⠀in⠀a⠀household⠀note⠀or⠀a⠀reply⠀to⠀a⠀request.\n\nLet⠀timing⠀and⠀the⠀material⠀conditions⠀of⠀writing⠀matter.⠀A⠀letter⠀may⠀arrive⠀too⠀late,⠀be⠀left⠀unsent,⠀be⠀read⠀by⠀the⠀wrong⠀person,⠀or⠀be⠀answered⠀after⠀circumstances⠀have⠀changed.⠀Gaps⠀between⠀documents⠀can⠀carry⠀as⠀much⠀meaning⠀as⠀the⠀documents⠀themselves.⠀Keep⠀readable⠀continuity⠀by⠀letting⠀each⠀new⠀record⠀respond⠀to⠀the⠀previous⠀one⠀or⠀to⠀an⠀event⠀the⠀reader⠀can⠀infer,⠀without⠀a⠀narrator⠀stepping⠀in⠀to⠀reconcile⠀every⠀conflict.⠀The⠀relationship's⠀outcome⠀may⠀remain⠀uncertain,⠀with⠀the⠀documents⠀showing⠀the⠀characters'⠀changing⠀positions⠀rather⠀than⠀a⠀final⠀verdict.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamakaf::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Fluffy⠀/⠀Comforting\n\nSpend⠀attention⠀on⠀chosen⠀kindness⠀and⠀familiar⠀preferences.⠀Use⠀the⠀Austen⠀profile's⠀social⠀precision⠀to⠀make⠀comfort⠀specific:⠀a⠀character⠀remembers⠀how⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀takes⠀their⠀tea,⠀notices⠀that⠀they⠀are⠀tired⠀before⠀they⠀say⠀so,⠀chooses⠀a⠀seat⠀near⠀them⠀without⠀making⠀a⠀fuss,⠀or⠀performs⠀a⠀small⠀practical⠀service⠀that⠀eases⠀the⠀day.⠀Let⠀these⠀acts⠀carry⠀social⠀meaning—courtesy,⠀consideration,⠀and⠀the⠀quiet⠀claim⠀of⠀belonging—without⠀requiring⠀the⠀characters⠀to⠀announce⠀their⠀feelings.\n\nKeep⠀affection⠀sincere⠀and⠀observable.⠀The⠀viewpoint⠀character⠀may⠀register⠀warmth⠀through⠀the⠀other⠀person's⠀attention:⠀a⠀question⠀asked⠀at⠀the⠀right⠀moment,⠀an⠀errand⠀done⠀without⠀being⠀requested,⠀a⠀remembered⠀preference⠀offered⠀as⠀a⠀small⠀gift.⠀Free⠀indirect⠀judgment⠀may⠀show⠀the⠀character⠀interpreting⠀these⠀gestures⠀as⠀signs⠀of⠀care,⠀but⠀keep⠀that⠀reasoning⠀owned⠀by⠀the⠀character⠀rather⠀than⠀a⠀narrator's⠀guarantee.⠀The⠀other⠀person's⠀motive⠀may⠀be⠀exactly⠀what⠀it⠀appears,⠀and⠀the⠀scene⠀may⠀simply⠀let⠀the⠀characters⠀enjoy⠀each⠀other's⠀company.\n\nPreserve⠀personality,⠀privacy,⠀and⠀manageable⠀friction.⠀A⠀character⠀may⠀be⠀particular⠀about⠀their⠀habits,⠀need⠀time⠀alone,⠀or⠀disagree⠀about⠀a⠀minor⠀practical⠀matter⠀without⠀the⠀disagreement⠀threatening⠀the⠀relationship.⠀Comfort⠀does⠀not⠀make⠀everyone⠀agreeable,⠀and⠀established⠀problems⠀in⠀the⠀world⠀remain⠀present⠀even⠀when⠀the⠀scene⠀focuses⠀on⠀ease.⠀Let⠀the⠀friction⠀be⠀small⠀enough⠀to⠀coexist⠀with⠀warmth:⠀a⠀teasing⠀remark,⠀a⠀difference⠀in⠀preference,⠀a⠀moment⠀of⠀mild⠀embarrassment⠀that⠀passes.\n\nLet⠀the⠀romance⠀develop⠀through⠀the⠀accumulation⠀of⠀these⠀small⠀moments.⠀Attention⠀becomes⠀familiarity,⠀familiarity⠀becomes⠀trust,⠀and⠀trust⠀becomes⠀a⠀decision⠀to⠀keep⠀choosing⠀each⠀other's⠀company.⠀The⠀scene⠀need⠀not⠀reach⠀a⠀confession⠀or⠀a⠀resolution;⠀it⠀may⠀simply⠀end⠀with⠀the⠀characters⠀more⠀at⠀ease⠀together⠀than⠀they⠀were⠀before.⠀Keep⠀the⠀prose⠀warm⠀but⠀precise,⠀with⠀the⠀Austen⠀profile's⠀social⠀observation⠀giving⠀the⠀comfort⠀its⠀particular⠀shape⠀rather⠀than⠀dissolving⠀into⠀generic⠀sweetness.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamakag::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Formal⠀Literary⠀Novel\n\nWrite⠀in⠀composed⠀novel⠀prose⠀with⠀deliberate⠀transitions⠀and⠀sustained⠀paragraph⠀movement.⠀Distinguish⠀the⠀narration⠀from⠀ordinary⠀spoken⠀language:⠀the⠀sentences⠀may⠀be⠀more⠀measured,⠀the⠀connections⠀more⠀explicit,⠀and⠀the⠀social⠀context⠀more⠀fully⠀drawn⠀than⠀in⠀conversation.⠀Use⠀enough⠀narrative⠀distance⠀to⠀frame⠀a⠀scene⠀through⠀its⠀social⠀setting,⠀family⠀history,⠀or⠀the⠀community's⠀judgment⠀where⠀the⠀chosen⠀narrator⠀permits⠀it.⠀A⠀visit,⠀a⠀letter,⠀a⠀public⠀gathering,⠀or⠀a⠀private⠀conversation⠀may⠀be⠀introduced⠀with⠀the⠀circumstances⠀that⠀give⠀it⠀weight.\n\nApply⠀the⠀Austen⠀profile's⠀social⠀interpretation⠀through⠀the⠀narration's⠀attention⠀to⠀courtesy,⠀offers,⠀omissions,⠀money,⠀family,⠀and⠀reputation.⠀Let⠀a⠀small⠀exchange⠀carry⠀several⠀meanings,⠀and⠀use⠀free⠀indirect⠀judgment⠀to⠀follow⠀the⠀viewpoint⠀character's⠀reasoning⠀as⠀they⠀interpret⠀another⠀person's⠀behavior.⠀Keep⠀that⠀reasoning⠀owned⠀by⠀the⠀character:⠀the⠀narrator⠀may⠀frame⠀the⠀scene⠀and⠀supply⠀context,⠀but⠀the⠀character's⠀inference⠀is⠀not⠀the⠀narrator's⠀verdict.⠀Measured⠀irony⠀may⠀arise⠀from⠀the⠀contrast⠀between⠀what⠀a⠀character⠀believes⠀and⠀what⠀the⠀scene⠀reveals,⠀without⠀making⠀the⠀narration⠀uniformly⠀mocking.\n\nDevelop⠀the⠀romance⠀through⠀the⠀genre's⠀particular⠀mechanisms⠀rendered⠀with⠀formal⠀care.⠀Attention⠀may⠀be⠀shown⠀in⠀a⠀character's⠀sustained⠀observation⠀of⠀another⠀person's⠀habits.⠀Memory⠀may⠀be⠀given⠀a⠀full⠀paragraph,⠀with⠀the⠀past⠀event's⠀social⠀meaning⠀examined.⠀Proximity⠀may⠀be⠀arranged⠀by⠀family⠀obligation⠀or⠀social⠀occasion,⠀with⠀the⠀characters⠀aware⠀of⠀what⠀their⠀nearness⠀signifies⠀to⠀others.⠀Disclosure⠀may⠀occur⠀in⠀a⠀conversation⠀whose⠀formal⠀setting⠀makes⠀the⠀admission⠀more⠀consequential.⠀Disagreement⠀may⠀be⠀conducted⠀with⠀elaborate⠀courtesy⠀while⠀the⠀private⠀stakes⠀remain⠀visible⠀in⠀the⠀narration.⠀Care⠀may⠀appear⠀in⠀a⠀practical⠀arrangement⠀whose⠀social⠀implications⠀the⠀characters⠀understand.\n\nLet⠀timing,⠀obligations,⠀and⠀competing⠀wants⠀create⠀meaningful⠀complications.⠀The⠀narration⠀may⠀pause⠀to⠀explain⠀why⠀a⠀particular⠀moment⠀matters,⠀what⠀a⠀character⠀stands⠀to⠀lose,⠀or⠀how⠀a⠀family's⠀circumstances⠀constrain⠀a⠀choice.⠀Use⠀ceremony,⠀correspondence,⠀or⠀public/private⠀contrast⠀to⠀organize⠀a⠀passage⠀when⠀relevant,⠀but⠀do⠀not⠀impose⠀an⠀aristocratic⠀setting⠀or⠀archaic⠀vocabulary.⠀The⠀formal⠀architecture⠀is⠀the⠀style;⠀the⠀social⠀world⠀remains⠀whatever⠀the⠀active⠀story⠀supplies.⠀The⠀relationship's⠀outcome⠀need⠀not⠀be⠀settled⠀within⠀the⠀passage,⠀but⠀the⠀narration⠀should⠀make⠀the⠀characters'⠀positions⠀and⠀the⠀weight⠀of⠀their⠀choices⠀legible.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamakah::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Framed⠀Oral⠀Storytelling⠀(Arabian⠀Nights-inspired)\n\nWrite⠀the⠀romance⠀as⠀a⠀sequence⠀of⠀told⠀stories⠀in⠀which⠀each⠀telling⠀is⠀a⠀courtship⠀move.⠀Begin⠀each⠀embedded⠀tale⠀from⠀a⠀present⠀occasion⠀in⠀the⠀outer⠀scene.⠀Establish⠀why⠀this⠀teller⠀speaks⠀now⠀and⠀to⠀this⠀particular⠀listener.⠀Give⠀the⠀teller⠀one⠀concrete⠀social⠀cost⠀or⠀hope⠀carried⠀by⠀the⠀telling:⠀a⠀decision⠀delayed,⠀a⠀refusal⠀softened,⠀an⠀old⠀attachment⠀explained,⠀a⠀rival⠀warned⠀against,⠀or⠀a⠀question⠀the⠀teller⠀cannot⠀ask⠀directly.⠀Make⠀that⠀cost⠀legible⠀through⠀an⠀outer-scene⠀detail⠀immediately⠀before⠀the⠀tale⠀begins—a⠀debt⠀mentioned,⠀a⠀family⠀obligation⠀pressing,⠀a⠀silence⠀that⠀would⠀otherwise⠀be⠀filled—so⠀the⠀tale⠀is⠀not⠀merely⠀decorative.\n\nConstruct⠀each⠀embedded⠀tale⠀from⠀the⠀listener's⠀known⠀concerns⠀and⠀the⠀teller's⠀partial⠀self-portrait.⠀The⠀teller⠀selects,⠀flatters,⠀omits,⠀or⠀quietly⠀admits⠀according⠀to⠀what⠀they⠀want⠀the⠀listener⠀to⠀conclude.⠀While⠀composing⠀the⠀tale,⠀give⠀the⠀teller⠀one⠀specific⠀omission⠀that⠀they⠀believe⠀the⠀listener⠀will⠀not⠀notice,⠀and⠀one⠀specific⠀parallel⠀to⠀the⠀outer⠀situation⠀that⠀they⠀hope⠀the⠀listener⠀will⠀read.⠀Do⠀not⠀announce⠀either⠀directly⠀in⠀the⠀telling.⠀Instead,⠀let⠀the⠀tale's⠀arrangement⠀reveal⠀them:⠀a⠀repeated⠀phrase⠀attached⠀to⠀the⠀omitted⠀fact,⠀a⠀named⠀character⠀who⠀resembles⠀the⠀listener,⠀a⠀practical⠀detail⠀that⠀mirrors⠀the⠀outer⠀difficulty.\n\nUse⠀Austen's⠀social⠀interpretation⠀inside⠀both⠀levels.⠀Courtesy,⠀money,⠀family⠀obligation,⠀reputation,⠀and⠀small⠀breaches⠀of⠀manners⠀each⠀carry⠀more⠀than⠀one⠀meaning.⠀Free⠀indirect⠀judgment⠀belongs⠀to⠀a⠀clear⠀owner.⠀During⠀the⠀tale,⠀the⠀teller⠀may⠀privately⠀register⠀that⠀the⠀listener⠀has⠀missed⠀the⠀teller's⠀intended⠀point,⠀or⠀the⠀listener⠀may⠀privately⠀correct⠀the⠀teller's⠀self-portrait.⠀Let⠀the⠀narration⠀stay⠀close⠀enough⠀to⠀these⠀focal⠀assessments⠀that⠀the⠀reader⠀can⠀see⠀the⠀judgment⠀as⠀the⠀character's⠀own,⠀never⠀as⠀an⠀announced⠀truth.⠀In⠀the⠀outer⠀scene,⠀a⠀courteous⠀phrase⠀may⠀be⠀a⠀test,⠀a⠀delay,⠀or⠀a⠀genuine⠀gesture;⠀show⠀the⠀listener⠀noticing⠀which⠀it⠀seems⠀and⠀why.\n\nAt⠀the⠀threshold⠀back⠀into⠀the⠀outer⠀scene,⠀let⠀the⠀teller's⠀final⠀sentence⠀land⠀on⠀the⠀one⠀detail⠀of⠀the⠀tale⠀that⠀corresponds⠀to⠀the⠀outer⠀difficulty—a⠀phrasing,⠀an⠀amount,⠀a⠀repeated⠀object,⠀a⠀choice.⠀Do⠀not⠀explain⠀the⠀correspondence.⠀Write⠀the⠀listener's⠀immediate⠀response⠀first⠀as⠀a⠀visible⠀social⠀act:⠀a⠀praise,⠀a⠀counter-question,⠀a⠀practical⠀objection,⠀an⠀offer,⠀or⠀a⠀silence⠀held⠀too⠀long.⠀Then⠀decide⠀whether⠀that⠀response⠀continues⠀the⠀courtship⠀or⠀halts⠀it⠀at⠀this⠀occasion.⠀A⠀listener⠀who⠀asks⠀about⠀the⠀omitted⠀detail,⠀supplies⠀a⠀counter-story,⠀or⠀returns⠀to⠀the⠀outer⠀concern⠀shows⠀the⠀telling⠀has⠀worked.⠀A⠀listener⠀who⠀praises⠀the⠀tale's⠀elegance⠀while⠀ignoring⠀its⠀warning⠀shows⠀the⠀telling⠀has⠀failed,⠀and⠀the⠀failure⠀becomes⠀the⠀next⠀relationship⠀beat.\n\nKeep⠀the⠀narrative⠀levels⠀intelligible⠀by⠀marking⠀each⠀movement⠀in⠀and⠀out⠀of⠀the⠀tale⠀with⠀a⠀brief⠀outer-scene⠀indicator—a⠀pause,⠀a⠀gesture,⠀the⠀room's⠀return.⠀Let⠀repeated⠀objects,⠀names,⠀and⠀phrases⠀accrue⠀meaning⠀across⠀tellings,⠀but⠀do⠀not⠀make⠀them⠀truth⠀certificates;⠀they⠀should⠀help⠀the⠀reader⠀compare⠀what⠀each⠀person⠀heard.⠀Never⠀import⠀a⠀magical⠀bargain,⠀a⠀royal⠀court,⠀or⠀a⠀djinn⠀merely⠀to⠀mark⠀this⠀style.⠀Stop⠀at⠀a⠀natural⠀boundary:⠀an⠀embedded⠀tale⠀left⠀unfinished⠀because⠀the⠀outer⠀occasion⠀intervened,⠀a⠀completed⠀tale⠀as⠀the⠀listener's⠀answer⠀begins,⠀or⠀a⠀central⠀exchange⠀of⠀the⠀outer⠀scene⠀concluded.⠀Do⠀not⠀manufacture⠀a⠀cliffhanger⠀or⠀a⠀forced⠀revelation.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamakai::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀German-Language⠀Literary⠀Traditions\n\nWrite⠀the⠀romance⠀through⠀the⠀social-developmental⠀realism⠀route.⠀Choose⠀one⠀binding⠀material⠀fact⠀at⠀the⠀start—a⠀lease,⠀an⠀inheritance,⠀a⠀family⠀claim,⠀an⠀income⠀source,⠀a⠀debt,⠀a⠀work⠀obligation—and⠀let⠀it⠀determine⠀what⠀one⠀focal⠀character⠀can⠀risk,⠀admit,⠀or⠀postpone⠀in⠀the⠀relationship.⠀Do⠀not⠀let⠀this⠀fact⠀become⠀mere⠀stage⠀furniture.⠀Show⠀its⠀first⠀visible⠀effect⠀before⠀the⠀attraction⠀begins:⠀a⠀visit⠀canceled,⠀a⠀room⠀shared,⠀an⠀offer⠀declined,⠀or⠀a⠀piece⠀of⠀information⠀withheld⠀for⠀practical⠀reasons.⠀That⠀initial⠀effect⠀later⠀becomes⠀the⠀reader's⠀yardstick⠀for⠀how⠀the⠀relationship⠀has⠀changed.\n\nReturn⠀to⠀the⠀same⠀social⠀question⠀at⠀least⠀twice⠀in⠀different⠀settings—a⠀duty,⠀an⠀expense,⠀a⠀family⠀request,⠀a⠀choice⠀between⠀appearing⠀well⠀and⠀telling⠀the⠀truth.⠀On⠀the⠀first⠀return,⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀repeats⠀the⠀earlier⠀decision,⠀using⠀nearly⠀the⠀same⠀words,⠀and⠀privately⠀believes⠀the⠀repetition⠀is⠀still⠀necessary.⠀On⠀the⠀second⠀return,⠀they⠀change⠀the⠀response⠀because⠀they⠀now⠀understand⠀the⠀other⠀person's⠀position⠀differently.⠀Let⠀the⠀exact⠀repeated⠀phrase⠀appear⠀in⠀both⠀places.⠀The⠀reader⠀should⠀compare⠀the⠀phrase's⠀wording,⠀not⠀be⠀told⠀what⠀changed;⠀the⠀surrounding⠀circumstances⠀and⠀the⠀focal⠀character's⠀shifting⠀free⠀indirect⠀commentary⠀will⠀show⠀the⠀development.\n\nUse⠀Austen's⠀free⠀indirect⠀judgment⠀as⠀the⠀instrument⠀of⠀that⠀development.⠀The⠀narration⠀may⠀render⠀the⠀focal⠀character's⠀self-assessment⠀in⠀their⠀own⠀idiom,⠀then⠀let⠀a⠀small⠀concrete⠀detail—a⠀word⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀uses,⠀a⠀hesitation,⠀a⠀look,⠀a⠀family⠀member's⠀correction—expose⠀a⠀gap⠀between⠀that⠀self-assessment⠀and⠀what⠀the⠀situation⠀reveals.⠀Keep⠀the⠀judgment⠀owned⠀by⠀the⠀character.⠀When⠀their⠀understanding⠀changes,⠀the⠀free⠀indirect⠀prose⠀should⠀become⠀less⠀self-justifying⠀without⠀announcing⠀the⠀improvement.⠀The⠀other⠀party⠀in⠀the⠀romance⠀must⠀have⠀their⠀own⠀material⠀life⠀and⠀their⠀own⠀reasons⠀for⠀hesitation.⠀Before⠀any⠀significant⠀confession⠀or⠀offer,⠀impose⠀a⠀concrete⠀competing⠀obligation⠀on⠀that⠀person⠀as⠀well:⠀a⠀job⠀that⠀demands⠀departure,⠀a⠀family⠀member⠀who⠀needs⠀support,⠀a⠀reputation⠀that⠀would⠀suffer.⠀Show⠀that⠀the⠀two⠀people⠀are⠀negotiating⠀costs,⠀not⠀that⠀one⠀is⠀a⠀reward⠀for⠀the⠀other's⠀growth.\n\nLet⠀attraction,⠀trust,⠀and⠀vulnerability⠀emerge⠀from⠀particular⠀exchanges:⠀an⠀unexpected⠀candor⠀during⠀a⠀shared⠀task,⠀a⠀disagreement⠀about⠀what⠀can⠀be⠀said⠀in⠀company,⠀an⠀offer⠀of⠀help⠀that⠀costs⠀something.⠀Prose⠀rhythm⠀follows⠀the⠀interpretation:⠀use⠀longer⠀sentences⠀when⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀is⠀reasoning⠀about⠀duty⠀or⠀revising⠀an⠀earlier⠀self-image,⠀and⠀shorter⠀sentences⠀for⠀decisive⠀action,⠀embarrassment,⠀or⠀a⠀curt⠀refusal.⠀The⠀setting,⠀language,⠀and⠀community⠀come⠀from⠀the⠀story⠀actually⠀supplied;⠀this⠀route⠀does⠀not⠀relocate⠀the⠀cast⠀or⠀require⠀a⠀particular⠀country.⠀End⠀at⠀a⠀natural⠀boundary⠀in⠀a⠀repeated⠀situation⠀or⠀an⠀aftermath.⠀Do⠀not⠀announce⠀whether⠀the⠀couple⠀belongs⠀together;⠀show⠀what⠀belonging⠀would⠀cost⠀and⠀what⠀each⠀is⠀prepared⠀to⠀pay⠀at⠀this⠀point.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamakaj::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Gothic-Punk\n\nWrite⠀the⠀romance⠀as⠀an⠀intimate⠀collision⠀between⠀inherited⠀authority⠀and⠀present⠀life.⠀Choose⠀one⠀concrete⠀inherited⠀structure—family⠀property,⠀an⠀institution,⠀an⠀old⠀debt,⠀a⠀social⠀obligation—and⠀keep⠀it⠀present⠀in⠀every⠀scene⠀through⠀at⠀least⠀one⠀itemized⠀urban⠀detail:⠀a⠀worn⠀stairwell,⠀a⠀locked⠀office,⠀a⠀borrowed⠀room,⠀a⠀late⠀train,⠀a⠀thin⠀partition.⠀The⠀detail⠀works⠀only⠀if⠀it⠀affects⠀the⠀encounter,⠀not⠀merely⠀decorates⠀it.⠀A⠀locked⠀office⠀can⠀make⠀a⠀question⠀impossible⠀to⠀ask;⠀a⠀late⠀train⠀can⠀force⠀a⠀choice⠀between⠀being⠀seen⠀and⠀being⠀sincere.\n\nMake⠀masks⠀legible⠀with⠀Austen's⠀social⠀interpretation.⠀When⠀a⠀character⠀performs⠀courtesy,⠀deference,⠀competence,⠀or⠀indifference,⠀show⠀at⠀least⠀one⠀specific⠀toll⠀the⠀performance⠀exacts:⠀a⠀phrase⠀that⠀cannot⠀be⠀said,⠀a⠀person⠀who⠀must⠀not⠀be⠀acknowledged,⠀a⠀debt⠀that⠀must⠀not⠀be⠀named.⠀Free⠀indirect⠀judgment⠀should⠀let⠀the⠀reader⠀see⠀a⠀focal⠀character⠀privately⠀read⠀their⠀own⠀mask⠀or⠀someone⠀else's,⠀but⠀keep⠀the⠀judgment⠀owned⠀by⠀that⠀character.⠀Do⠀not⠀make⠀every⠀mask⠀sinister;⠀some⠀are⠀survival,⠀some⠀are⠀kindness,⠀and⠀some⠀are⠀the⠀price⠀of⠀belonging.\n\nLet⠀private⠀desire⠀develop⠀through⠀the⠀gothic-punk⠀intimacy⠀of⠀masks.⠀Track⠀one⠀exact⠀phrase,⠀gesture,⠀or⠀object⠀that⠀appears⠀only⠀while⠀a⠀mask⠀is⠀in⠀place.⠀Let⠀that⠀phrase⠀be⠀used⠀in⠀a⠀later⠀private⠀scene⠀in⠀a⠀changed⠀tone⠀or⠀with⠀a⠀different⠀object,⠀so⠀the⠀reader⠀can⠀mark⠀that⠀the⠀mask⠀has⠀shifted.⠀A⠀mask⠀falls⠀away⠀only⠀after⠀an⠀earned⠀exchange—shared⠀risk,⠀a⠀disclosure⠀that⠀could⠀be⠀used⠀as⠀a⠀weapon,⠀help⠀that⠀costs⠀the⠀helper⠀something.⠀When⠀it⠀falls,⠀show⠀the⠀aftermath⠀in⠀the⠀release⠀of⠀one⠀specific⠀piece⠀of⠀previously⠀unavailable⠀knowledge:⠀what⠀the⠀mask⠀was⠀buying,⠀who⠀the⠀character⠀feared⠀seeing⠀it⠀fall,⠀or⠀what⠀they⠀believed⠀would⠀happen⠀if⠀it⠀did.⠀The⠀other⠀person's⠀response⠀may⠀be⠀relief,⠀confusion,⠀or⠀new⠀caution,⠀but⠀do⠀not⠀automatically⠀reward⠀the⠀unmasking.⠀It⠀may⠀now⠀cost⠀both⠀people⠀something⠀concrete.\n\nAlways⠀protect⠀actual⠀knowledge⠀permissions.⠀While⠀one⠀character⠀is⠀masked,⠀do⠀not⠀enter⠀the⠀other⠀person's⠀private⠀certainty⠀about⠀what⠀the⠀mask⠀conceals⠀unless⠀that⠀character⠀has⠀been⠀given⠀a⠀concrete⠀observable⠀basis⠀for⠀the⠀inference.⠀When⠀the⠀story⠀reaches⠀a⠀moment⠀of⠀genuine⠀disclosure,⠀the⠀other⠀person's⠀interiority⠀may⠀briefly⠀open;⠀otherwise,⠀keep⠀their⠀private⠀state⠀offstage.⠀Preserve⠀the⠀portable⠀gothic-punk⠀treatment⠀without⠀importing⠀Kindred⠀physiology,⠀factions,⠀powers,⠀or⠀blood-bond⠀rules.⠀The⠀inherited⠀structure⠀is⠀a⠀human⠀arrangement⠀with⠀human⠀costs.⠀Stop⠀at⠀a⠀natural⠀boundary:⠀the⠀completion⠀of⠀an⠀unmasking,⠀the⠀revision⠀of⠀one⠀phrase,⠀or⠀a⠀charged⠀practical⠀breakdown⠀in⠀city⠀space.⠀Do⠀not⠀force⠀the⠀next⠀date,⠀the⠀next⠀test,⠀or⠀the⠀next⠀revelation.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamakak::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Indian⠀Literary⠀Traditions\n\nWrite⠀the⠀romance⠀through⠀the⠀social-domestic⠀realism⠀route.⠀Choose⠀one⠀family⠀claim⠀that⠀binds⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀before⠀the⠀attraction⠀appears—an⠀elder's⠀need,⠀an⠀expected⠀marriage,⠀a⠀sibling's⠀education,⠀a⠀house⠀that⠀cannot⠀be⠀sold—and⠀one⠀domestic⠀object⠀through⠀which⠀that⠀claim⠀is⠀regularly⠀enacted:⠀a⠀debt⠀ledger,⠀a⠀tea⠀tray,⠀a⠀shared⠀room,⠀a⠀wedding⠀arrangement,⠀a⠀bus⠀ticket,⠀a⠀portion⠀of⠀food.⠀Whenever⠀the⠀romance⠀advances,⠀return⠀to⠀that⠀object⠀in⠀a⠀new⠀mood.⠀The⠀first⠀appearance⠀establishes⠀obligation;⠀the⠀second⠀shows⠀hesitation;⠀a⠀later⠀appearance⠀shows⠀the⠀character⠀privately⠀comparing⠀the⠀claim⠀with⠀the⠀person⠀they⠀want.⠀The⠀object's⠀reuse⠀does⠀not⠀have⠀to⠀be⠀announced;⠀let⠀the⠀reader⠀notice⠀the⠀changed⠀handling.\n\nUse⠀Austen's⠀social⠀interpretation⠀on⠀the⠀tiny⠀domestic⠀exchanges.⠀Before⠀any⠀inward⠀interpretation,⠀write⠀the⠀exact⠀domestic⠀act:⠀a⠀question⠀about⠀a⠀job,⠀a⠀remark⠀about⠀a⠀neighbor's⠀marriage,⠀an⠀offer⠀of⠀food,⠀a⠀silence⠀at⠀the⠀right⠀moment,⠀a⠀family⠀member's⠀careful⠀omission.⠀Then⠀give⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀a⠀specific,⠀owned⠀reading⠀of⠀that⠀act.⠀The⠀narration⠀may⠀show⠀the⠀character⠀misreading⠀courtesy⠀as⠀encouragement⠀or⠀recognizing⠀manipulation⠀without⠀being⠀able⠀to⠀name⠀it⠀aloud.⠀Do⠀not⠀explain⠀the⠀act's⠀meaning⠀in⠀narrative⠀voice.⠀Let⠀the⠀next⠀domestic⠀scene⠀revise⠀or⠀confirm⠀the⠀earlier⠀reading⠀through⠀another⠀concrete⠀act.\n\nThe⠀other⠀party⠀in⠀the⠀romance⠀must⠀carry⠀a⠀comparable⠀family⠀or⠀material⠀obligation⠀that⠀competes⠀with⠀the⠀attraction.⠀Give⠀that⠀obligation⠀one⠀visible⠀consequence⠀in⠀the⠀shared⠀story:⠀a⠀visit⠀cut⠀short,⠀a⠀job⠀far⠀away,⠀a⠀promise⠀made⠀before⠀they⠀met,⠀a⠀parent⠀they⠀cannot⠀leave.⠀When⠀the⠀romance⠀reaches⠀a⠀moment⠀of⠀strong⠀feeling,⠀make⠀the⠀other⠀party's⠀competing⠀obligation⠀impose⠀a⠀specific⠀cost⠀on⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀too.⠀That⠀cost⠀is⠀not⠀a⠀convenience;⠀it⠀changes⠀what⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀feels⠀able⠀to⠀say⠀or⠀do⠀next.\n\nKeep⠀language,⠀region,⠀community,⠀and⠀period⠀specific⠀from⠀the⠀story's⠀own⠀supplies,⠀without⠀adding⠀forced⠀English,⠀code-switching,⠀religion,⠀caste⠀collision,⠀or⠀a⠀generic⠀family⠀structure.⠀A⠀concrete⠀domestic⠀setting⠀is⠀enough;⠀do⠀not⠀append⠀a⠀cultural⠀glossary.⠀Attraction,⠀trust,⠀and⠀vulnerability⠀emerge⠀from⠀repeated⠀ordinary⠀negotiations:⠀who⠀supports⠀whom,⠀what⠀can⠀be⠀said⠀before⠀elders⠀or⠀neighbors,⠀what⠀a⠀person⠀may⠀choose⠀without⠀losing⠀their⠀place.⠀End⠀at⠀a⠀natural⠀boundary⠀in⠀a⠀domestic⠀scene⠀or⠀its⠀aftermath.⠀Do⠀not⠀decide⠀whether⠀the⠀couple⠀belongs⠀together;⠀show⠀what⠀belonging⠀would⠀cost⠀and⠀what⠀each⠀person⠀can⠀currently⠀pay.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamakal::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Japanese⠀Literary⠀Traditions\n\nWrite⠀the⠀romance⠀as⠀social⠀and⠀psychological⠀realism⠀with⠀a⠀closely⠀held⠀focal⠀narration.⠀Stay⠀near⠀one⠀character's⠀attention⠀for⠀a⠀stretch⠀at⠀a⠀time:⠀what⠀that⠀person⠀notices⠀in⠀company,⠀corrects⠀in⠀private⠀afterward,⠀and⠀cannot⠀yet⠀say.⠀Let⠀circumstance⠀power⠀the⠀restraint⠀—⠀a⠀family⠀expectation,⠀a⠀workplace⠀hierarchy,⠀a⠀debt⠀of⠀gratitude,⠀the⠀risk⠀of⠀misreading⠀a⠀single⠀gesture⠀—⠀so⠀that⠀holding⠀back⠀is⠀a⠀live⠀choice⠀with⠀a⠀reason⠀behind⠀it.⠀Give⠀each⠀character⠀a⠀manner⠀of⠀their⠀own:⠀one⠀may⠀be⠀blunt⠀with⠀everyone⠀except⠀this⠀person,⠀another⠀may⠀perform⠀cheerfulness⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀has⠀to⠀read⠀past.\n\nMake⠀omission⠀the⠀main⠀channel⠀of⠀feeling.⠀In⠀company,⠀track⠀what⠀a⠀character⠀almost⠀says,⠀asks⠀twice,⠀answers⠀a⠀beat⠀late,⠀or⠀replaces⠀with⠀a⠀courtesy.⠀Afterward,⠀in⠀a⠀private⠀interval⠀—⠀the⠀walk⠀home,⠀the⠀quiet⠀after⠀the⠀house⠀settles⠀—⠀let⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀rehearse⠀the⠀exchange⠀and⠀revise⠀it:⠀regretting⠀a⠀flat⠀reply,⠀discovering⠀that⠀an⠀offer⠀was⠀personal⠀rather⠀than⠀dutiful,⠀weighing⠀a⠀favor⠀that⠀now⠀has⠀to⠀be⠀repaid.⠀Own⠀every⠀judgment⠀in⠀that⠀character's⠀voice.⠀The⠀narration⠀may⠀be⠀wry⠀about⠀them,⠀but⠀it⠀does⠀not⠀announce⠀verdicts⠀about⠀people⠀in⠀general.\n\nBuild⠀by⠀recurrence⠀rather⠀than⠀reversal.⠀Return⠀the⠀pair⠀to⠀a⠀place,⠀an⠀errand,⠀or⠀a⠀social⠀formula⠀—⠀the⠀same⠀counter,⠀the⠀same⠀monthly⠀dinner,⠀the⠀same⠀exchange⠀of⠀thanks⠀—⠀and⠀let⠀the⠀seasons⠀mark⠀the⠀distance⠀between⠀visits.⠀Blossom⠀or⠀rain⠀outside⠀a⠀familiar⠀window⠀works⠀as⠀a⠀clock,⠀not⠀decoration:⠀what⠀changes⠀is⠀how⠀much⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀reads⠀into⠀a⠀pause⠀there.⠀Let⠀small⠀disclosures⠀accumulate⠀—⠀a⠀remembered⠀detail⠀about⠀childhood,⠀an⠀admission⠀made⠀lightly⠀and⠀at⠀once⠀qualified,⠀a⠀question⠀asked⠀in⠀spring⠀and⠀answered⠀differently⠀in⠀autumn.\n\nKeep⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀partly⠀opaque,⠀with⠀a⠀practical⠀life⠀and⠀private⠀reasons⠀of⠀their⠀own.⠀Their⠀warmth⠀can⠀be⠀real⠀and⠀still⠀not⠀enough;⠀the⠀focal⠀character's⠀reading⠀of⠀it⠀can⠀be⠀wrong⠀now⠀and⠀corrected⠀later⠀by⠀something⠀small.⠀The⠀attachment⠀becomes⠀legible⠀through⠀comparison⠀across⠀these⠀returns,⠀not⠀through⠀a⠀sudden⠀declaration.⠀Stop⠀where⠀the⠀scene's⠀attention⠀naturally⠀rests⠀—⠀inside⠀an⠀unfinished⠀visit,⠀or⠀a⠀reflection⠀not⠀yet⠀concluded⠀—⠀without⠀forcing⠀a⠀confession,⠀a⠀parting,⠀or⠀a⠀cliffhanger.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamakam::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Latin⠀American⠀Literary⠀Traditions\n\nWrite⠀the⠀romance⠀as⠀intimate⠀urban⠀psychological⠀fiction⠀in⠀the⠀specific⠀city⠀the⠀story⠀supplies.⠀Ground⠀every⠀scene⠀in⠀the⠀material⠀facts⠀of⠀that⠀place⠀—⠀the⠀route⠀between⠀two⠀neighborhoods,⠀the⠀fare⠀and⠀the⠀hour⠀of⠀the⠀last⠀bus,⠀which⠀streets⠀belong⠀to⠀whom,⠀whose⠀window⠀faces⠀the⠀courtyard⠀—⠀and⠀make⠀those⠀facts⠀do⠀plot⠀work.⠀Distance⠀is⠀a⠀cost,⠀a⠀visit⠀competes⠀with⠀a⠀shift,⠀a⠀borrowed⠀room⠀offers⠀the⠀privacy⠀the⠀street⠀denies.⠀Keep⠀the⠀language,⠀community,⠀and⠀history⠀the⠀story⠀actually⠀gives,⠀and⠀keep⠀the⠀telling⠀realist:⠀nothing⠀supernatural⠀enters⠀a⠀world⠀that⠀excludes⠀it.\n\nTreat⠀the⠀surrounding⠀community⠀as⠀a⠀working⠀surveillance.⠀A⠀relative's⠀remark⠀at⠀a⠀family⠀dinner,⠀a⠀neighbor⠀who⠀reports⠀arrivals,⠀a⠀friend's⠀warning⠀dressed⠀as⠀concern,⠀a⠀landlord's⠀casual⠀question⠀—⠀each⠀one⠀changes⠀what⠀a⠀character⠀can⠀afford⠀to⠀admit,⠀to⠀themselves⠀as⠀much⠀as⠀to⠀the⠀other⠀person.⠀Split⠀the⠀pair's⠀registers⠀by⠀space:⠀warm⠀and⠀unfinished⠀in⠀a⠀kitchen⠀after⠀midnight,⠀careful⠀and⠀joking⠀on⠀the⠀pavement,⠀formal⠀under⠀a⠀relative's⠀eyes.⠀Let⠀the⠀same⠀sentence⠀mean⠀different⠀things⠀in⠀different⠀rooms,⠀and⠀stage⠀that⠀difference⠀instead⠀of⠀explaining⠀it.\n\nGive⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀the⠀interpretation.⠀In⠀close⠀free⠀indirect⠀prose,⠀let⠀them⠀privately⠀decode⠀these⠀pressures⠀—⠀recognizing⠀the⠀maneuver⠀inside⠀a⠀relative's⠀question,⠀mistaking⠀guardedness⠀for⠀indifference,⠀revising⠀an⠀opinion⠀of⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀after⠀a⠀second⠀meeting⠀at⠀the⠀market⠀—⠀sometimes⠀correctly,⠀sometimes⠀not,⠀with⠀consequences⠀either⠀way.⠀Keep⠀money⠀and⠀obligation⠀legible:⠀a⠀salary⠀shared⠀with⠀relatives,⠀a⠀debt⠀being⠀paid⠀off,⠀a⠀job⠀that⠀claims⠀the⠀hours⠀the⠀romance⠀needs.⠀Weigh⠀both⠀people's⠀claims⠀honestly;⠀an⠀ill⠀relative⠀and⠀a⠀plan⠀to⠀leave⠀the⠀city⠀are⠀real⠀claims⠀with⠀aftermath,⠀not⠀obstacles⠀staged⠀to⠀be⠀defeated.\n\nLet⠀the⠀attachment⠀build⠀through⠀urban⠀situations⠀the⠀reader⠀can⠀compare⠀—⠀the⠀same⠀bus⠀stop⠀in⠀different⠀weather,⠀the⠀same⠀family⠀gathering⠀a⠀season⠀apart⠀—⠀so⠀each⠀meeting⠀revises⠀the⠀last⠀impression.⠀Neither⠀marriage⠀nor⠀separation⠀is⠀owed;⠀the⠀subject⠀is⠀how⠀each⠀person⠀weighs⠀belonging⠀together⠀against⠀the⠀other⠀claims⠀on⠀their⠀life.⠀End⠀the⠀reply⠀where⠀the⠀scene's⠀attention⠀rests,⠀mid-errand⠀or⠀mid-reflection,⠀without⠀a⠀forced⠀resolution.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamakan::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Light⠀Novel\n\nWrite⠀the⠀romance⠀in⠀fast,⠀clean⠀scenes⠀with⠀strong⠀visual⠀staging.⠀Enter⠀each⠀situation⠀directly:⠀within⠀the⠀first⠀few⠀lines⠀establish⠀the⠀room⠀or⠀street,⠀who⠀else⠀is⠀present,⠀and⠀the⠀practical⠀matter⠀at⠀hand⠀—⠀a⠀shift⠀about⠀to⠀start,⠀a⠀group⠀outing⠀already⠀assembled,⠀an⠀errand⠀that⠀must⠀be⠀finished⠀tonight.⠀Give⠀every⠀move⠀to⠀a⠀new⠀space⠀its⠀own⠀paragraph,⠀and⠀break⠀paragraphs⠀around⠀action,⠀dialogue,⠀and⠀private⠀response⠀so⠀the⠀reader⠀can⠀track⠀at⠀a⠀glance⠀what⠀happened,⠀what⠀was⠀said,⠀and⠀what⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀makes⠀of⠀it.\n\nLet⠀small⠀social⠀exchanges⠀carry⠀the⠀weight.⠀A⠀greeting⠀returned⠀a⠀beat⠀late,⠀a⠀seat⠀taken⠀or⠀avoided,⠀an⠀offer⠀of⠀a⠀ride,⠀a⠀question⠀about⠀family⠀answered⠀too⠀smoothly,⠀the⠀one⠀name⠀that⠀goes⠀unmentioned⠀—⠀each⠀can⠀signal⠀affection,⠀caution,⠀obligation,⠀or⠀self-deception⠀without⠀the⠀narration⠀saying⠀which.⠀Follow⠀a⠀significant⠀exchange⠀with⠀a⠀reaction⠀beat⠀that⠀does⠀real⠀interpretive⠀work:⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀notices⠀what⠀was⠀odd,⠀recalls⠀a⠀parallel⠀from⠀an⠀earlier⠀scene,⠀corrects⠀a⠀first⠀impression,⠀or⠀catches⠀themselves⠀performing⠀composure.⠀Keep⠀the⠀judgment⠀in⠀that⠀character's⠀hands,⠀so⠀the⠀same⠀cue⠀can⠀be⠀misread⠀now⠀and⠀understood⠀later.⠀A⠀reaction⠀may⠀be⠀serious,⠀uncertain,⠀angry,⠀or⠀funny⠀according⠀to⠀who⠀is⠀having⠀it;⠀wit⠀belongs⠀to⠀particular⠀people,⠀not⠀to⠀every⠀line.\n\nStage⠀the⠀social⠀field⠀visually.⠀Who⠀sits⠀nearest⠀whom,⠀who⠀checks⠀a⠀phone⠀and⠀who⠀doesn't,⠀what⠀gets⠀served,⠀how⠀far⠀apart⠀two⠀people⠀stand⠀while⠀a⠀third⠀watches⠀—⠀these⠀visible⠀arrangements⠀carry⠀the⠀meaning⠀that⠀manners⠀conceal.⠀When⠀an⠀unfamiliar⠀name⠀or⠀mechanic⠀matters,⠀present⠀it⠀clearly⠀in⠀a⠀sentence⠀or⠀two⠀inside⠀the⠀scene,⠀without⠀glossary⠀padding.\n\nGive⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀an⠀offstage⠀practical⠀life⠀that⠀explains⠀their⠀hesitations⠀—⠀hours,⠀family,⠀money,⠀another⠀obligation⠀—⠀so⠀the⠀relationship⠀reads⠀as⠀a⠀negotiation⠀between⠀two⠀people⠀rather⠀than⠀a⠀prize⠀for⠀one⠀person's⠀feelings.⠀End⠀the⠀reply⠀where⠀the⠀scene's⠀attention⠀rests:⠀mid-conversation,⠀just⠀after⠀a⠀reaction⠀beat,⠀or⠀on⠀an⠀unsettled⠀arrangement,⠀not⠀on⠀a⠀staged⠀confession⠀or⠀cliffhanger.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPamakao::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Romance⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Lyrical⠀Prose\n\nWrite⠀the⠀developing⠀romance⠀through⠀a⠀sustained⠀lyrical⠀attention⠀that⠀follows⠀the⠀focal⠀character's⠀social⠀perception.⠀When⠀an⠀exchange⠀carries⠀multiple⠀meanings—a⠀courtesy⠀masking⠀a⠀claim,⠀a⠀question⠀probing⠀an⠀omission,⠀an⠀offer⠀burdened⠀by⠀family⠀expectation—let⠀the⠀sentence⠀or⠀paragraph⠀expand⠀in⠀step⠀with⠀the⠀character's⠀dawning⠀understanding.⠀The⠀syntax⠀itself⠀should⠀enact⠀the⠀process⠀of⠀seeing⠀more:⠀begin⠀with⠀the⠀visible⠀gesture,⠀then⠀move⠀into⠀what⠀it⠀implies,⠀what⠀it⠀would⠀cost⠀to⠀respond,⠀and⠀what⠀remains⠀withheld.⠀Use⠀rhythm⠀and⠀sound⠀to⠀register⠀shifts⠀in⠀the⠀character's⠀attention,⠀but⠀keep⠀the⠀figurative⠀language⠀tied⠀to⠀what⠀the⠀character⠀actually⠀notices⠀in⠀the⠀scene.\n\nDevelop⠀recurring⠀images⠀as⠀instruments⠀of⠀social⠀and⠀emotional⠀interpretation.⠀An⠀object⠀or⠀sensory⠀detail⠀first⠀observed⠀in⠀one⠀context—the⠀arrangement⠀of⠀a⠀room,⠀the⠀pause⠀before⠀an⠀answer,⠀the⠀texture⠀of⠀a⠀letter,⠀a⠀particular⠀phrase—may⠀return⠀in⠀a⠀later⠀scene⠀when⠀the⠀relationship⠀has⠀altered.⠀When⠀the⠀narrator⠀revisits⠀an⠀image,⠀its⠀changed⠀resonance⠀should⠀reveal⠀what⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀now⠀understands⠀about⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀or⠀about⠀her⠀own⠀position.⠀Avoid⠀assigning⠀every⠀character⠀the⠀narrator's⠀lyrical⠀register;⠀their⠀speech⠀should⠀keep⠀its⠀own⠀rhythm⠀and⠀directness.\n\nPreserve⠀Austen's⠀judged⠀interiority⠀through⠀free⠀indirect⠀thought⠀that⠀belongs⠀to⠀the⠀focal⠀character,⠀not⠀to⠀an⠀omniscient⠀moralist.⠀The⠀prose⠀can⠀render⠀a⠀character's⠀confident⠀self-description⠀and⠀then